window.SECTIONS=window.SECTIONS||[];window.SECTIONS.push({"id":"grammaire","name":"Grammaire progressive","short":"Grammaire","color":"#3F8F63","blurb":"All 60 chapters and 8 bilans. Chapters 1–14 keep the transcribed examples and the scans. From chapter 15 on, each chapter is an original lesson with examples and interactive drills. The printed answer key is not copied.","lessons":[{"id":"gr-1","label":"Chapitre 1","name":"Vous êtes japonais ?","summary":"La présentation. Je suis + name, nationality, job — and why French drops the article before a profession.","art":null,"groups":[{"name":"La présentation","note":"Two rules this chapter rests on. <strong>Always use je suis or je m'appelle</strong> — never a bare name. And <strong>no article before a profession</strong>: <em>je suis médecin</em>, never <em>je suis un médecin</em>. That one catches every English speaker.","items":[["Bonjour, je suis Kenji Takashi.","bohn-ZHOOR, zhuh swee","Hello, I'm Kenji Takashi."],["Je m'appelle Kenji Takashi.","zhuh ma-PELL","My name is Kenji Takashi."],["Vous êtes japonais ? — Oui, je suis japonais.","voo-ZET zha-po-NAY","Are you Japanese? — Yes, I am."],["Vous êtes médecin ? — Non, je suis chimiste.","voo-ZET mayd-SAN — nohn, zhuh swee shee-MEEST","Are you a doctor? — No, I'm a chemist."],["Je suis français. Je suis professeur.","zhuh swee frahn-SAY. zhuh swee pro-fess-UR","I'm French. I'm a teacher."],["Jean, vous êtes professeur ou étudiant ?","zhahn, voo-ZET pro-fess-UR oo zay-tew-dee-AHN","Jean, are you a teacher or a student?"],["Kenji, vous êtes médecin ou chimiste ?","voo-ZET mayd-SAN oo shee-MEEST","Kenji, are you a doctor or a chemist?"],["Bip, vous êtes astronaute ou professeur ?","voo-ZET zas-tro-NOTE oo pro-fess-UR","Bip, are you an astronaut or a teacher?"]]},{"name":"Pratiquer le chapitre 1","quiz":[{"t":"choice","q":"A job takes no article.","opts":["Je suis un médecin.","Je suis médecin."],"a":"Je suis médecin."},{"t":"cloze","q":"___ m'appelle Inès.","a":"Je"},{"t":"translate","q":"I am French.","a":"Je suis français.","alt":["Je suis française."]},{"t":"cloze","q":"Vous ___ japonais ?","a":"êtes"},{"t":"choice","q":"Are you a student?","opts":["Vous êtes étudiant ?","Vous êtes un étudiant ?"],"a":"Vous êtes étudiant ?"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}],"bookpages":["g008","g009"]},{"id":"gr-2","label":"Chapitre 2","name":"Il est grand. Elle est grande.","summary":"Masculine to feminine. Add -e and the silent consonant wakes up — that's how you hear gender.","art":"agreement","groups":[{"name":"Masculin → féminin","cols":"two","note":"<strong>Féminin = masculin + -e.</strong> The point of that -e: a silent final consonant becomes audible, so you can <em>hear</em> the gender. Words already ending in -e (jeune, russe, calme) don't change.","items":[["français → française","frahn-SAY → frahn-SEZ","French"],["portugais → portugaise","por-tew-GAY → por-tew-GEZ","Portuguese"],["suédois → suédoise","sway-DWAH → sway-DWAZ","Swedish"],["chinois → chinoise","shee-NWAH → shee-NWAZ","Chinese"],["mexicain → mexicaine","mek-see-KAN → mek-see-KEN","Mexican"],["américain → américaine","a-may-ree-KAN → a-may-ree-KEN","American"],["autrichien → autrichienne","oh-tree-shee-AN → oh-tree-shee-EN","Austrian"],["canadien → canadienne","ka-na-dee-AN → ka-na-dee-EN","Canadian"],["coréen → coréenne","ko-ray-AN → ko-ray-EN","Korean"],["allemand → allemande","al-MAHN → al-MAHND","German"],["espagnol → espagnole","es-pan-YOL → es-pan-YOL","Spanish"],["russe → russe","rewss → rewss","Russian — identical"],["grec → grecque","grek → grek","Greek — irregular"],["turc → turque","tewrk → tewrk","Turkish — irregular"],["étudiant → étudiante","ay-tew-dee-AHN → ay-tew-dee-AHNT","student"],["grand → grande","GRAHN → GRAHND","tall"],["blond → blonde","BLOHN → BLOHND","blond"],["marié → mariée","ma-ree-AY → ma-ree-AY","married"],["petit → petite","puh-TEE → puh-TEET","small"],["vert → verte","VAIR → VAIRT","green"],["amusant → amusante","a-mew-ZAHN → a-mew-ZAHNT","funny"],["intelligent → intelligente","an-tel-ee-ZHAHN → an-tel-ee-ZHAHNT","intelligent"],["souriant → souriante","soo-ree-AHN → soo-ree-AHNT","smiling"],["jeune → jeune","ZHUHN → ZHUHN","young — no change"]]},{"name":"Les autres terminaisons","cols":"two","note":"<strong>-on → -onne</strong> · <strong>-er → -ère</strong> · <strong>-eur / -eux → -euse</strong> · <strong>-teur → -trice</strong> for most professions.<br><br>One exception: <strong>chanteur → chanteuse</strong>, not chantrice. And some jobs never change: <strong>professeur, médecin, écrivain, auteur</strong> stay identical — though professeure, écrivaine and auteure are increasingly used.","items":[["bon → bonne","bohn → bun","good"],["breton → bretonne","bruh-TOHN → bruh-TUN","Breton"],["mignon → mignonne","meen-YOHN → meen-YUN","cute"],["étranger → étrangère","ay-trahn-ZHAY → ay-trahn-ZHAIR","foreign"],["boulanger → boulangère","boo-lahn-ZHAY → boo-lahn-ZHAIR","baker"],["infirmier → infirmière","an-feer-mee-AY → an-feer-mee-AIR","nurse"],["poissonnier → poissonnière","pwa-son-YAY → pwa-son-YAIR","fishmonger"],["serveur → serveuse","sair-VUR → sair-VUZ","waiter"],["danseur → danseuse","dahn-SUR → dahn-SUHZ","dancer"],["menteur → menteuse","mahn-TUR → mahn-TUZ","liar"],["heureux → heureuse","uh-RUH → uh-RUZ","happy"],["acteur → actrice","ak-TUR → ak-TREESS","actor"],["instituteur → institutrice","an-stee-tew-TUR → an-stee-tew-TREESS","primary teacher"],["présentateur → présentatrice","pray-zahn-ta-TUR → pray-zahn-ta-TREESS","presenter"],["chanteur → chanteuse","shahn-TUR → shahn-TUHZ","singer — the exception"],["professeur → professeur","pro-fess-UR","teacher — unchanged"],["médecin → médecin","mayd-SAN","doctor — unchanged"],["beau → belle","BO → BELL","beautiful"],["gros → grosse","GRO → GROSS","big / fat"],["vieux → vieille","vee-UH → vee-AY-yuh","old"],["gentil → gentille","zhahn-TEE → zhahn-TEE-yuh","kind"],["blanc → blanche","BLAHN → BLAHNSH","white"]]},{"name":"Pratiquer le chapitre 2","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"Il est grand. Elle est ___.","a":"grande"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Il est intelligent. Elle est ___.","a":"intelligente"},{"t":"choice","q":"A happy woman.","opts":["Elle est heureux.","Elle est heureuse."],"a":"Elle est heureuse."},{"t":"translate","q":"She is small.","a":"Elle est petite."},{"t":"cloze","q":"Marc est sportif. Léa est ___.","a":"sportive"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}],"bookpages":["g010","g011","g012","g013"]},{"id":"gr-3","label":"Chapitre 3","name":"Ils sont grands.","summary":"Singular to plural — add -s, unless the word already ends in -s or -x.","art":null,"groups":[{"name":"Singulier → pluriel","cols":"two","note":"<strong>Pluriel = singulier + -s.</strong> But a masculine word already ending in <strong>-s</strong> or <strong>-x</strong> doesn't change at all. One irregular: <em>beau → beaux</em>.<br><br>And when a group is mixed, the masculine plural always wins — one man among ten women still makes it <strong>ils</strong>.","items":[["il est blond → ils sont blonds","eel ay BLOHN → eel sohn BLOHN","he is / they are blond"],["elle est blonde → elles sont blondes","el ay BLOHND → el sohn BLOHND","she is / they are blonde"],["il est étudiant → ils sont étudiants","eel et ay-tew-dee-AHN → eel sohn tay-tew-dee-AHN","student(s)"],["il est français → ils sont français","eel ay frahn-SAY → eel sohn frahn-SAY","French — no change"],["il est vieux → ils sont vieux","eel ay vee-UH → eel sohn vee-UH","old — no change"],["il est beau → ils sont beaux","eel ay BO → eel sohn BO","handsome — irregular"],["Ils sont américains.","eel sohn ta-may-ree-KAN","They're American."],["Elles sont brésiliennes.","el sohn bray-zeel-YEN","They're Brazilian. (fem.)"],["Elles sont danseuses.","el sohn dahn-SUHZ","They're dancers. (fem.)"],["Ils sont gentils.","eel sohn zhahn-TEE","They're kind."],["Elles sont gentilles.","el sohn zhahn-TEE-yuh","They're kind. (fem.)"],["Elles sont célibataires.","el sohn say-lee-ba-TAIR","They're single. (fem.)"]]},{"name":"Pratiquer le chapitre 3","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"Il est grand. Ils sont ___.","a":"grands"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Elle est petite. Elles sont ___.","a":"petites"},{"t":"choice","q":"The books are interesting.","opts":["Les livres sont intéressant.","Les livres sont intéressants."],"a":"Les livres sont intéressants."},{"t":"translate","q":"They (women) are tired.","a":"Elles sont fatiguées."},{"t":"cloze","q":"un hôtel moderne → des hôtels ___.","a":"modernes"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}],"bookpages":["g014","g015"]},{"id":"gr-4","label":"Chapitre 4","name":"Je suis, tu es, il est…","summary":"Être in full, the tu/vous decision, and the two very different jobs of on.","art":null,"groups":[{"name":"Être, tu/vous, on","note":"<strong>vous</strong> does two jobs: polite singular, and plural of any register. <strong>tu</strong> is familiar singular only.<br><br><strong>on</strong> also does two: casual 'we' (<em>Jean et moi, on est fatigués</em>) and general 'people' (<em>Quand on est enrhumé, on est fatigué</em>). It always conjugates like <em>il</em>.","items":[["Vous êtes prêt, monsieur Meyer ?","voo-ZET PREH, muh-syuh may-AIR","Are you ready, Mr Meyer? (polite)"],["Tu es prêt, papa ?","tew ay PREH, pa-PAH","Are you ready, dad? (familiar)"],["Vous êtes prêts ? (messieurs)","voo-ZET PREH","Are you ready? (several men)"],["Vous êtes prêtes ? (mesdames)","voo-ZET PRET","Are you ready? (several women)"],["Jean et moi, on est enrhumés.","zhahn ay mwah, oh-nay tahn-rew-MAY","Jean and I have colds. (on = nous)"],["Quand on est enrhumé, on est fatigué.","kahn oh-nay tahn-rew-MAY, oh-nay fa-tee-GAY","When you have a cold, you're tired. (on = people)"],["Nous sommes contents d'être à Paris.","noo sum kohn-TAHN detr a pa-REE","We're happy to be in Paris."],["Nous sommes désolés d'être en retard.","noo sum day-zo-LAY detr ahn ruh-TAR","We're sorry to be late."],["Quand on est en vacances, on est content.","kahn oh-nay ahn va-KAHNSS, oh-nay kohn-TAHN","When you're on holiday, you're happy."],["Quand on est en retard, on est pressé.","kahn oh-nay ahn ruh-TAR, oh-nay press-AY","When you're late, you're in a hurry."]]},{"name":"Pratiquer le chapitre 4","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"Je ___, tu es, il est.","a":"suis"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Nous ___.","a":"sommes"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Vous ___.","a":"êtes"},{"t":"choice","q":"Polite or plural.","opts":["Tu es en retard.","Vous êtes en retard."],"a":"Vous êtes en retard."},{"t":"translate","q":"They are French.","a":"Ils sont français.","alt":["Elles sont françaises."]}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}],"bookpages":["g016","g017"]},{"id":"gr-5","label":"Chapitre 5","name":"Est-ce que… ? Non, je ne suis pas…","summary":"Three ways to ask a yes/no question, and where pas goes.","art":"nepas","groups":[{"name":"Poser une question","note":"Three ways to ask the same yes/no question: rising intonation alone, or <strong>est-ce que</strong> on the front. Both are normal in speech — est-ce que is the safer default while you're building confidence, because it signals 'question' from word one.","items":[["Vous êtes japonais.","voo-ZET zha-po-NAY","You're Japanese. (statement, falling tone)"],["Vous êtes japonais ?","voo-ZET zha-po-NAY","Are you Japanese? (rising tone)"],["Est-ce que vous êtes japonais ?","es-kuh voo-ZET zha-po-NAY","Are you Japanese? (with est-ce que)"],["Est-ce que Jean est français ?","es-kuh zhahn ay frahn-SAY","Is Jean French?"],["Est-ce que vous êtes étudiant ?","es-kuh voo-ZET zay-tew-dee-AHN","Are you a student?"],["Est-ce que tu es marié ?","es-kuh tew ay ma-ree-AY","Are you married?"],["Est-ce que Marco est blond ?","es-kuh mar-KO ay BLOHN","Is Marco blond?"]]},{"name":"La négation ne… pas","cols":"two","items":[["Je ne suis pas content.","zhuh nuh swee pah kohn-TAHN","I'm not happy."],["Elle n'est pas riche.","el nay pah REESH","She's not rich."],["Ils ne sont pas italiens.","eel nuh sohn pah zee-tal-YAN","They're not Italian."],["Je ne suis pas brun.","zhuh nuh swee pah BRUHN","I'm not dark-haired."],["Je ne suis pas français.","zhuh nuh swee pah frahn-SAY","I'm not French."],["Je ne suis pas professeur.","zhuh nuh swee pah pro-fess-UR","I'm not a teacher."],["Le lit n'est pas confortable.","luh LEE nay pah kohn-for-TAHB-luh","The bed isn't comfortable."],["L'eau n'est pas chaude.","lo nay pah SHOWD","The water isn't hot."],["Les chambres ne sont pas chères.","lay SHAHM-bruh nuh sohn pah SHAIR","The rooms aren't expensive."],["Non, il n'est pas blond. Il est brun.","nohn, eel nay pah BLOHN. eel ay BRUHN","No, he's not blond. He's dark-haired."]]},{"name":"Pratiquer le chapitre 5","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"___ tu es français ?","a":"Est-ce que"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Non, je ___ suis pas français.","a":"ne"},{"t":"choice","q":"A yes/no question.","opts":["Est-ce que vous habitez ici ?","Vous habitez ici est-ce que ?"],"a":"Est-ce que vous habitez ici ?"},{"t":"translate","q":"I am not tired.","a":"Je ne suis pas fatigué.","alt":["Je ne suis pas fatiguée."]},{"t":"cloze","q":"Elle n'est ___ là.","a":"pas"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}],"bookpages":["g018","g019"]},{"id":"gr-6","label":"Chapitre 6","name":"Je parle, je regarde, j'aime…","summary":"Regular -ER verbs — the biggest verb family in French, and the one that never lets you down.","art":null,"groups":[{"name":"Les verbes en -ER","cols":"two","note":"<strong>Drop -er, add -e.</strong> That final -e is silent — <em>je parle</em> is said zhuh PARL. And <strong>je → j'</strong> before a vowel or silent h.<br><br>This is the biggest verb family in French. Almost every new verb you meet will follow it.","items":[["parler → je parle","zhuh PARL","to speak → I speak"],["regarder → je regarde","zhuh ruh-GARD","to watch → I watch"],["manger → je mange","zhuh MAHNZH","to eat → I eat"],["travailler → je travaille","zhuh tra-VIGH","to work → I work"],["téléphoner → je téléphone","zhuh tay-lay-FON","to call → I call"],["écouter → j'écoute","zhay-KOOT","to listen → I listen"],["aimer → j'aime","zhem","to love → I love"],["habiter → j'habite","zha-BEET","to live → I live"],["étudier → j'étudie","zhay-tew-DEE","to study → I study"],["commencer → je commence","zhuh ko-MAHNSS","to start → I start"],["terminer → je termine","zhuh tair-MEEN","to finish → I finish"],["dîner → je dîne","zhuh DEEN","to have dinner → I have dinner"]]},{"name":"Une journée — le modèle","items":[["Je travaille dans une banque.","zhuh tra-vigh dahn zewn BAHNK","I work in a bank."],["Le matin, je commence à 9 heures.","luh ma-TAN, zhuh ko-MAHNSS a nuh-VUR","In the morning I start at 9."],["Le soir, je termine à 18 heures.","luh SWAHR, zhuh tair-MEEN a dee-zwee-TUR","In the evening I finish at 6."],["À midi, je mange à la cafétéria avec mes collègues.","a mee-DEE, zhuh MAHNZH a lah ka-fay-tay-REE-a a-vek may ko-LEG","At noon I eat in the cafeteria with my colleagues."],["Le soir, je dîne chez moi.","luh SWAHR, zhuh DEEN shay MWAH","In the evening I have dinner at home."],["Après le repas, je regarde la télévision ou j'écoute la radio.","a-PRAY luh ruh-PAH, zhuh ruh-GARD lah tay-lay-vee-zee-OHN oo zhay-KOOT lah ra-dee-O","After the meal I watch TV or listen to the radio."],["J'aime le sport et la musique.","zhem luh SPOR ay lah mew-ZEEK","I like sport and music."],["J'habite à Paris.","zha-BEET a pa-REE","I live in Paris."],["Je parle français.","zhuh parl frahn-SAY","I speak French."],["J'étudie l'anglais.","zhay-tew-DEE lahn-GLAY","I'm studying English."]]},{"name":"Pratiquer le chapitre 6","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"J'___ (habiter) à Paris.","a":"habite"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Je ___ (manger) à midi.","a":"mange"},{"t":"choice","q":"I like","opts":["j'aime","je aime"],"a":"j'aime"},{"t":"translate","q":"I speak a little French.","a":"Je parle un peu français."},{"t":"cloze","q":"J'___ (étudier) le soir.","a":"étudie"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}],"bookpages":["g020","g021"]},{"id":"gr-7","label":"Chapitre 7","name":"Je parle, tu parles, il parle…","summary":"Pages 22–23. The full present tense of -ER verbs, the two endings you can actually hear, on as a general subject, and a revision of questions and negation.","art":"erverbs","bookpages":["g022","g023"],"groups":[{"name":"Parler — les six personnes","cols":"two","items":[["Je parle français.","zhuh parl frahn-SAY","I speak French."],["Tu parles anglais.","tew parl ahn-GLAY","You speak English."],["Il / Elle / On parle russe.","eel / el / ohn parl REWSS","He / She / One speaks Russian."],["Nous parlons italien.","noo par-LOHN ee-tal-YAN","We speak Italian."],["Vous parlez chinois.","voo par-LAY shee-NWAH","You speak Chinese."],["Ils / Elles parlent allemand.","eel / el parl al-MAHN","They speak German."]]},{"name":"Les finales muettes — ce que vous n'entendez pas","note":"<strong>Four of the six forms sound identical.</strong> The endings <code>-e</code>, <code>-es</code> and <code>-ent</code> are all silent, so <em>je parle</em>, <em>tu parles</em>, <em>il parle</em> and <em>ils parlent</em> are one single sound: <strong>parl</strong>. Only the spelling tells them apart.","cols":"two","items":[["Je parle","zhuh PARL","silent -e"],["Tu parles","tew PARL","silent -es"],["Il / Elle / On parle","eel PARL","silent -e"],["Ils / Elles parlent","eel PARL","silent -ent"],["J'aime","ZHEM","silent -e"],["Tu aimes","tew EM","silent -es"],["Il / Elle / On aime","eel EM","silent -e"],["Ils / Elles aiment","eel ZEM","silent -ent, with liaison"]]},{"name":"Les finales sonores — ce que vous entendez","note":"Only <strong>-ons</strong> and <strong>-ez</strong> are pronounced. Those two forms are the only ones your ear can pick out.","cols":"two","items":[["Vous parlez","voo par-LAY","audible -ez"],["Nous parlons","noo par-LOHN","audible -ons"],["Vous aimez","voo zay-MAY","audible -ez, with liaison"],["Nous aimons","noo zay-MOHN","audible -ons, with liaison"]]},{"name":"« On » — rappel","note":"Two jobs, and the sentence tells you which. With named people it means <strong>nous</strong>; on its own it means <strong>people in general</strong>.","items":[["Igor et moi, on parle russe.","ee-GOR ay MWAH, ohn parl REWSS","Igor and I speak Russian. — on = nous"],["En Russie, on parle russe.","ahn rew-SEE, ohn parl REWSS","In Russia they speak Russian. — on = en général"]]},{"name":"L'interrogation et la négation — révision","cols":"two","items":[["Vous parlez anglais ?","voo par-LAY ahn-GLAY","Do you speak English?"],["Non, je ne parle pas anglais.","nohn, zhuh nuh parl pah zahn-GLAY","No, I don't speak English."],["Vous habitez en France ?","voo za-bee-TAY ahn FRAHNSS","Do you live in France?"],["Non, je n'habite pas en France.","nohn, zhuh na-BEET pah zahn FRAHNSS","No, I don't live in France."],["Est-ce que Marie travaille ?","es-kuh ma-REE tra-VIGH","Does Marie work?"],["Non, elle ne travaille pas.","nohn, el nuh tra-VIGH PAH","No, she doesn't work."],["Est-ce que Paul et Max étudient ?","es-kuh pol ay maks ay-TEW-dee","Do Paul and Max study?"],["Non, ils n'étudient pas.","nohn, eel nay-TEW-dee PAH","No, they don't study."]]},{"name":"Ex. 1 — moi, ma sœur, mes parents","note":"The verb endings for <em>je</em> and <em>elle</em> are both silent, so they sound identical — only the spelling changes.","items":[["J'habite dans le centre. / Elle habite en banlieue.","zha-BEET dahn luh SAHN-truh / el a-BEET ahn bahn-lee-UH","I live in the centre. / She lives in the suburbs."],["Je travaille dans une banque. / Elle travaille dans une librairie.","zhuh tra-VIGH dahn zewn BAHNK / el tra-VIGH dahn zewn lee-bray-REE","I work in a bank. / She works in a bookshop."],["Je commence à 9 heures. / Elle commence à 10 heures.","zhuh ko-MAHNSS a nuh VUR / el ko-MAHNSS a dee ZUR","I start at 9. / She starts at 10."],["Je termine à 17 heures. / Elle termine à 19 heures.","zhuh tair-MEEN a dee-set UR / el tair-MEEN a deez-nuh VUR","I finish at 5pm. / She finishes at 7pm."],["Je dîne à 20 heures. / Elle dîne à 21 heures.","zhuh DEEN a van TUR / el DEEN a van-tay-uh NUR","I have dinner at 8pm. / She dines at 9pm."],["Mes parents habitent en banlieue, ils travaillent dans une école.","may pa-RAHN a-BEET ahn bahn-lee-UH, eel tra-VIGH dahn zewn ay-KOL","A model third text, in the ils form."]]},{"name":"Ex. 2 — répondre avec « on »","items":[["Qu'est-ce qu'on fait dans une discothèque ? — On danse.","kes-koh FAY dahn zewn dees-ko-TEK ? — ohn DAHNSS","What do you do in a nightclub? — You dance."],["… dans une piscine ? — On nage.","… dahn zewn pee-SEEN ? — ohn NAHZH","… in a swimming pool? — You swim."],["… dans une cabine téléphonique ? — On téléphone.","… dahn zewn ka-BEEN tay-lay-fo-NEEK ? — ohn tay-lay-FON","… in a phone box? — You make a call."],["… dans un restaurant ? — On mange.","… dahn zuhn res-to-RAHN ? — ohn MAHNZH","… in a restaurant? — You eat."]]},{"name":"Ex. 3 — conjuguez les verbes","cols":"two","items":[["Je travaille. Vous travaillez. Nous travaillons.","zhuh tra-VIGH. voo tra-va-YAY. noo tra-va-YOHN","travailler — to work"],["Elle danse. Vous dansez. Nous dansons.","el DAHNSS. voo dahn-SAY. noo dahn-SOHN","danser — to dance"],["On fume. Vous fumez. Nous fumons.","ohn FEWM. voo few-MAY. noo few-MOHN","fumer — to smoke"],["Tu téléphones. Vous téléphonez. Nous téléphonons.","tew tay-lay-FON. voo tay-lay-fo-NAY. noo tay-lay-fo-NOHN","téléphoner — to phone"],["Ils dînent. Vous dînez. Nous dînons.","eel DEEN. voo dee-NAY. noo dee-NOHN","dîner — to have dinner"]]},{"name":"Ex. 4 — question et réponse négative","items":[["Tu fumes ? — Non, je ne fume pas.","tew FEWM ? — nohn, zhuh nuh fewm PAH","Do you smoke? — No, I don't."],["Tu danses ? — Non, je ne danse pas.","tew DAHNSS ? — nohn, zhuh nuh dahnss PAH","Do you dance? — No, I don't."],["Tu parles espagnol ? — Non, je ne parle pas espagnol.","tew parl es-pan-YOL ? — nohn, zhuh nuh parl pah zes-pan-YOL","Do you speak Spanish? — No, I don't."],["Tu aimes le rock ? — Non, je n'aime pas le rock.","tew em luh ROK ? — nohn, zhuh nem pah luh ROK","Do you like rock? — No, I don't."]]},{"name":"Ex. 5 — corriger d'après le texte","note":"The six statements at the top are the facts; each question contradicts one of them, so you answer in the negative and then give the true version.","items":[["Les enfants jouent dans leur chambre.","lay zahn-FAHN ZHOO dahn lur SHAHM-bruh","The children play in their bedroom."],["Le grand-père regarde un match à la télé.","luh grahn-PAIR ruh-GARD uhn MATCH a lah tay-LAY","Grandad is watching a match on TV."],["La grand-mère téléphone à sa sœur.","lah grahn-MAIR tay-lay-FON a sa SUR","Grandma is phoning her sister."],["La baby-sitter étudie le français.","lah ba-bee-see-TAIR ay-TEW-dee luh frahn-SAY","The babysitter is studying French."],["Les parents dînent au restaurant.","lay pa-RAHN DEEN oh res-to-RAHN","The parents are dining out."],["Le chat mange sur le balcon.","luh SHA mahnzh sewr luh bal-KOHN","The cat is eating on the balcony."],["Les enfants jouent dans le salon ? — Non, ils ne jouent pas dans le salon. Ils jouent dans leur chambre.","… nohn, eel nuh zhoo pah dahn luh sa-LOHN","Do the children play in the living room? — No, in their bedroom."],["La baby-sitter regarde la télévision ? — Non, elle ne regarde pas la télévision. Elle étudie le français.","… el nuh ruh-gard pah lah tay-lay-vee-zee-OHN","Is the babysitter watching TV? — No, she's studying French."],["Le grand-père écoute la radio ? — Non, il n'écoute pas la radio. Il regarde un match à la télé.","… eel nay-KOOT pah lah ra-dee-O","Is grandad listening to the radio? — No, he's watching a match."]]},{"name":"Le vocabulaire du chapitre","cols":"two","items":[["une banque","ewn BAHNK","a bank"],["une librairie","ewn lee-bray-REE","a bookshop"],["la banlieue","lah bahn-lee-UH","the suburbs"],["le centre","luh SAHN-truh","the centre"],["commencer","ko-mahn-SAY","to begin"],["terminer","tair-mee-NAY","to finish"],["dîner","dee-NAY","to dine"],["nager","na-ZHAY","to swim"],["fumer","few-MAY","to smoke"],["jouer","zhoo-AY","to play"],["une discothèque","ewn dees-ko-TEK","a nightclub"],["une piscine","ewn pee-SEEN","a swimming pool"],["une cabine téléphonique","ewn ka-BEEN tay-lay-fo-NEEK","a phone box"],["le salon","luh sa-LOHN","the living room"],["le balcon","luh bal-KOHN","the balcony"],["un match","uhn MATCH","a match"],["une baby-sitter","ewn ba-bee-see-TAIR","a babysitter"],["le chat","luh SHA","the cat"]]},{"name":"Pratiquer le chapitre 7","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"Tu ___ (parler) anglais ?","a":"parles"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Nous ___ (habiter) ici.","a":"habitons"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Ils ___ (aimer) le foot.","a":"aiment"},{"t":"translate","q":"Do you (vous) live in Lyon?","a":"Vous habitez à Lyon ?","alt":["Est-ce que vous habitez à Lyon ?"]},{"t":"choice","q":"she works","opts":["elle travaille","elle travaillent"],"a":"elle travaille"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-8","label":"Chapitre 8","name":"J'achète, vous achetez. Je préfère, vous préférez.","summary":"Pages 24–25. The -ER verbs that shift their spelling: accents that appear and vanish, doubled consonants, and the -ger and -cer verbs that protect their soft sound.","art":"particularites","bookpages":["g024","g025"],"groups":[{"name":"Le dialogue de la page","items":[["Vous préférez les noires ou les blanches ?","voo pray-fay-RAY lay NWAHR oo lay BLAHNSH","Do you prefer the black ones or the white ones?"],["Je préfère les blanches.","zhuh pray-FAIR lay BLAHNSH","I prefer the white ones."]]},{"name":"Accent grave — préférer","note":"<strong>The rule behind it:</strong> the ending is silent in four forms, so the vowel before it has to carry the sound and takes an <strong>accent grave (è)</strong>. In <em>nous</em> and <em>vous</em> the ending is pronounced, so the <strong>é</strong> stays.<br><br>Same pattern: <em>espérer, répéter, compléter</em>.","cols":"two","items":[["Je préfère","zhuh pray-FAIR","è — ending silent"],["Tu préfères","tew pray-FAIR","è"],["Il préfère","eel pray-FAIR","è"],["Ils préfèrent","eel pray-FAIR","è"],["Nous préférons","noo pray-fay-ROHN","é — ending audible"],["Vous préférez","voo pray-fay-RAY","é — ending audible"],["espérer","es-pay-RAY","to hope"],["répéter","ray-pay-TAY","to repeat"],["compléter","kohm-play-TAY","to complete"]]},{"name":"Accent grave — acheter","note":"Here the infinitive has <strong>no accent at all</strong>; the è appears only where the ending falls silent. Same pattern: <em>mener, amener, emmener, enlever, peser</em>.","cols":"two","items":[["J'achète","zha-SHET","è"],["Tu achètes","tew a-SHET","è"],["Il achète","eel a-SHET","è"],["Ils achètent","eel za-SHET","è"],["Nous achetons","noo zash-TOHN","plain e"],["Vous achetez","voo zash-TAY","plain e"],["mener","muh-NAY","to lead"],["amener","am-NAY","to bring (a person)"],["emmener","ahm-NAY","to take (a person) along"],["enlever","ahn-luh-VAY","to remove"],["peser","puh-ZAY","to weigh"]]},{"name":"Consonne doublée — jeter, appeler","note":"Instead of an accent, these double the consonant to keep the vowel open — <strong>tt</strong> and <strong>ll</strong> where the ending is silent, single letter where it is heard.","cols":"two","items":[["Je jette","zhuh ZHET","tt"],["Tu jettes","tew ZHET","tt"],["Il jette","eel ZHET","tt"],["Ils jettent","eel ZHET","tt"],["Nous jetons","noo zhuh-TOHN","single t"],["Vous jetez","voo zhuh-TAY","single t"],["J'appelle","zha-PELL","ll"],["Tu appelles","tew a-PELL","ll"],["Il appelle","eel a-PELL","ll"],["Ils appellent","eel za-PELL","ll"],["Nous appelons","noo za-play-OHN","single l"],["Vous appelez","voo za-play-AY","single l"]]},{"name":"Verbes en -ayer et -oyer","cols":"two","items":[["Je paie / je paye","zhuh PAY","I pay — both spellings allowed"],["Vous payez","voo pay-YAY","you pay"],["J'envoie","zhahn-VWAH","I send"],["Vous envoyez","voo zahn-vwa-YAY","you send"]]},{"name":"Verbes en -ger et -cer — la finale -ons","note":"Before the <strong>-ons</strong> ending, <em>g</em> and <em>c</em> would harden. French keeps them soft by adding a silent <strong>e</strong> after g, and a <strong>cédille</strong> under c.","cols":"two","items":[["Je mange / Nous mangeons","zhuh MAHNZH / noo mahn-ZHOHN","g + e + ons"],["Je voyage / Nous voyageons","zhuh vwa-YAHZH / noo vwa-ya-ZHOHN","g + e + ons"],["changer / nous changeons","shahn-ZHAY / noo shahn-ZHOHN","to change"],["nager / nous nageons","na-ZHAY / noo na-ZHOHN","to swim"],["partager / nous partageons","par-ta-ZHAY / noo par-ta-ZHOHN","to share"],["Je commence / Nous commençons","zhuh ko-MAHNSS / noo ko-mahn-SOHN","ç + ons"],["J'avance / Nous avançons","zha-VAHNSS / noo za-vahn-SOHN","ç + ons"]]},{"name":"Ex. 1 — préférences","items":[["Vous préférez les pâtes ou le riz ? — Je préfère le riz.","voo pray-fay-RAY lay PAHT oo luh REE ? — zhuh pray-FAIR luh REE","Do you prefer pasta or rice? — I prefer rice."],["Vous préférez le printemps ou l'automne ? — Je préfère le printemps.","… luh pran-TAHN oo lo-TUN","Spring or autumn?"],["Vous préférez le vin blanc ou le vin rouge ? — Je préfère le vin rouge.","… luh van BLAHN oo luh van ROOZH","White wine or red?"]]},{"name":"Ex. 2 — mettre les accents","note":"Accent only where the ending is silent. Nos 5, 6, 7, 8 and 9 are <em>nous</em> or <em>vous</em> forms, so they keep the plain vowel.","cols":"two","items":[["1. J'achète un livre.","zha-SHET uhn LEE-vruh","è"],["2. Tu amènes des amis.","tew a-MEN day za-MEE","è"],["3. Je préfère les blondes.","zhuh pray-FAIR lay BLOHND","è"],["4. Elle répète la leçon.","el ray-PET lah luh-SOHN","è"],["5. Vous préférez les brunes.","voo pray-fay-RAY lay BREWN","no change"],["6. Nous enlevons nos chaussures.","noo zahn-luh-VOHN no sho-SEWR","no change"],["7. Vous répétez les phrases.","voo ray-pay-TAY lay FRAZ","no change"],["8. Nous complétons la leçon.","noo kohm-play-TOHN lah luh-SOHN","no change"],["9. Nous achetons un livre.","noo zash-TOHN uhn LEE-vruh","no change"],["10. Il pèse 100 kilos.","eel PEZ sahn kee-LO","è"],["11. On répète les phrases.","ohn ray-PET lay FRAZ","è"],["12. Ils préfèrent les rousses.","eel pray-FAIR lay ROOSS","è"]]},{"name":"Ex. 3 — complétez","items":[["1. J'appelle Londres. Vous appelez Prague. Ils appellent Rio.","zha-PELL … voo za-play-AY … eel za-PELL","appeler"],["2. Il achète une veste. Elle achète une robe. Nous achetons un pull.","eel a-SHET … noo zash-TOHN","acheter"],["3. Tu appelles ta sœur. Nous appelons nos amis. Vous appelez vos parents.","tew a-PELL … noo za-play-OHN … voo za-play-AY","appeler"],["4. Vous mangez une glace. Elle mange des frites. Nous mangeons un sandwich.","voo mahn-ZHAY … noo mahn-ZHOHN","manger"],["5. Vous voyagez en avion. Ils voyagent en train. Nous voyageons en car.","voo vwa-ya-ZHAY … noo vwa-ya-ZHOHN","voyager"]]},{"name":"Ex. 4 — Bip et Zaza racontent","note":"The whole text moved from <em>je</em> to <em>nous</em> — which is where the -ger spelling changes show up.","items":[["Nous visitons de nombreuses planètes.","noo vee-zee-TOHN duh nohm-BRUHZ pla-NET","We visit many planets."],["Nous voyageons en astronef.","noo vwa-ya-ZHOHN ah nas-tro-NEF","We travel by spaceship. — note the e"],["Quand nous arrivons dans un nouveau pays, nous achetons un dictionnaire et nous étudions la langue.","kahn noo za-ree-VOHN … noo zash-TOHN … noo zay-tew-dee-OHN","When we arrive in a new country we buy a dictionary and study the language."],["Nous posons des questions.","noo po-ZOHN day kes-tee-OHN","We ask questions."],["Nous goûtons la nourriture. Nous comparons.","noo goo-TOHN lah noo-ree-TEWR. noo kohm-pa-ROHN","We taste the food. We compare."],["De temps en temps, nous appelons Mars.","duh tahn zahn TAHN, noo za-play-OHN MARSS","From time to time we call Mars."],["Nous aimons beaucoup la France. Nous espérons revenir un jour.","noo zay-MOHN bo-KOO lah FRAHNSS. noo zes-pay-ROHN ruh-vuh-NEER uhn ZHOOR","We love France. We hope to come back one day."]]},{"name":"Ex. 5 — énumérez les activités","items":[["Au marché, je regarde, je compare et j'achète.","oh mar-SHAY, zhuh ruh-GARD, zhuh kohm-PAR ay zha-SHET","At the market I look, compare and buy."],["À l'école maternelle, les enfants dansent, chantent et jouent.","a lay-KOL ma-tair-NELL, lay zahn-FAHN DAHNSS, SHAHNT ay ZHOO","At nursery school the children dance, sing and play."],["Dans la classe de langue, nous parlons, nous écoutons et nous répétons.","dahn lah klahss duh LAHNG, noo par-LOHN, noo zay-koo-TOHN ay noo ray-pay-TOHN","In the language class we speak, listen and repeat."],["Dans notre société de consommation, on achète, on jette et on achète.","dahn NOT-ruh so-see-ay-TAY duh kohn-so-ma-see-OHN, ohn a-SHET, ohn ZHET ay ohn a-SHET","In our consumer society we buy, throw away and buy again."]]},{"name":"Le vocabulaire du chapitre","cols":"two","items":[["préférer","pray-fay-RAY","to prefer"],["acheter","ash-TAY","to buy"],["jeter","zhuh-TAY","to throw away"],["appeler","ap-LAY","to call"],["payer","pay-YAY","to pay"],["envoyer","ahn-vwa-YAY","to send"],["voyager","vwa-ya-ZHAY","to travel"],["goûter","goo-TAY","to taste"],["comparer","kohm-pa-RAY","to compare"],["poser une question","po-ZAY ewn kes-tee-OHN","to ask a question"],["une veste","ewn VEST","a jacket"],["une robe","ewn ROB","a dress"],["un pull","uhn PEWL","a jumper"],["des chaussures","day sho-SEWR","shoes"],["les pâtes","lay PAHT","pasta"],["le riz","luh REE","rice"],["une glace","ewn GLAHSS","an ice cream"],["des frites","day FREET","chips"],["le printemps","luh pran-TAHN","spring"],["l'automne","lo-TUN","autumn"],["le vin blanc / rouge","luh van BLAHN / ROOZH","white / red wine"],["une planète","ewn pla-NET","a planet"],["un astronef","uh nas-tro-NEF","a spaceship"],["la nourriture","lah noo-ree-TEWR","food"],["un dictionnaire","uhn deek-see-o-NAIR","a dictionary"],["l'école maternelle","lay-KOL ma-tair-NELL","nursery school"],["la société de consommation","lah so-see-ay-TAY duh kohn-so-ma-see-OHN","consumer society"],["blond / brun / roux","BLOHN / BRUHN / ROO","blond / brown-haired / red-haired"]]},{"name":"Pratiquer le chapitre 8","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"J'___ (acheter) du pain.","a":"achète"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Nous ___ (acheter) du pain.","a":"achetons"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Je ___ (préférer) le thé.","a":"préfère"},{"t":"choice","q":"we prefer","opts":["nous préférez","nous préférons"],"a":"nous préférons"},{"t":"translate","q":"She buys a book.","a":"Elle achète un livre."}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-9","label":"Chapitre 9","name":"Je me lave. Je me regarde.","summary":"Pages 26–27. Reflexive verbs — when the subject is also the object, and the little pronoun that has to sit in front of the verb.","art":"reflexif","bookpages":["g026","g027"],"groups":[{"name":"La différence en images","note":"When the subject is <strong>also the object</strong> of the verb, French uses a reflexive pronoun. <em>me</em> means <em>moi-même</em> — myself.","cols":"two","items":[["Je lave ma voiture.","zhuh LAHV ma vwa-TEWR","I wash my car. — object is the car"],["Je me lave.","zhuh muh LAHV","I wash myself."],["Je regarde la télé.","zhuh ruh-GARD lah tay-LAY","I watch TV. — object is the TV"],["Je me regarde.","zhuh muh ruh-GARD","I look at myself."]]},{"name":"Se laver — les pronoms réfléchis","cols":"two","note":"The pronoun always goes <strong>in front of the verb</strong>, never after it.","items":[["Je me lave","zhuh muh LAHV","I wash (myself)"],["Tu te laves","tew tuh LAHV","you wash"],["Il / Elle / On se lave","eel suh LAHV","he / she washes"],["Nous nous lavons","noo noo la-VOHN","we wash"],["Vous vous lavez","voo voo la-VAY","you wash"],["Ils / Elles se lavent","eel suh LAHV","they wash"]]},{"name":"À ne pas dire","note":"✓ Dites : <strong>Je me regarde.</strong> &nbsp;✗ Ne dites pas : <s>Je regarde moi.</s>","items":[["Je me regarde.","zhuh muh ruh-GARD","I look at myself. — correct"]]},{"name":"Élision et liaison","note":"<strong>me → m'</strong>, <strong>te → t'</strong>, <strong>se → s'</strong> before a vowel or a silent h. And in <em>nous nous</em> / <em>vous vous</em> the second word links with a <strong>z</strong> sound.","cols":"two","items":[["Je m'appelle","zhuh ma-PELL","I'm called"],["Tu t'habilles","tew ta-BEE-yuh","you get dressed"],["Il s'ennuie","eel sahn-NWEE","he is bored"],["Nous nous amusons","noo noo za-mew-ZOHN","we enjoy ourselves — liaison z"],["Vous vous ennuyez","voo voo zahn-nwee-YAY","you are bored — liaison z"]]},{"name":"Ex. 1 — le modèle","items":[["Le lundi, je me lève à sept heures et demie et je me couche à dix heures.","luh luhn-DEE, zhuh muh LEV a set UR ay duh-MEE ay zhuh muh KOOSH a dee ZUR","On Mondays I get up at 7.30 and go to bed at 10."],["Le samedi, je me lève à neuf heures et je me couche à minuit.","luh sam-DEE … a nuh VUR … a mee-NWEE","On Saturdays I get up at 9 and go to bed at midnight."],["Le dimanche, je me lève à onze heures.","luh dee-MAHNSH, zhuh muh LEV a ohn ZUR","On Sundays I get up at 11."]]},{"name":"Ex. 2 — les habitudes de Bruno et de ses parents","items":[["En semaine, il se lève à sept heures.","ahn suh-MEN, eel suh LEV a set UR","During the week he gets up at 7."],["En vacances, il se lève à onze heures.","ahn va-KAHNSS, eel suh LEV a ohn ZUR","On holiday he gets up at 11."],["Ses parents se lèvent à six heures et ils se couchent tôt.","say pa-RAHN suh LEV a see ZUR ay eel suh KOOSH TOH","His parents get up at 6 and go to bed early."]]},{"name":"Ex. 3 — quand on est…","items":[["Quand on est fatigué, on se repose.","kahn ohn ay fa-tee-GAY, ohn suh ruh-POZ","When you're tired, you rest."],["Quand on a sommeil, on se couche.","kahn ohn a so-MAY, ohn suh KOOSH","When you're sleepy, you go to bed."],["Quand on est sale, on se lave.","kahn ohn ay SAL, ohn suh LAHV","When you're dirty, you wash."],["Quand on est mouillé, on se sèche.","kahn ohn ay moo-YAY, ohn suh SESH","When you're wet, you dry off."],["Quand il fait beau, on se promène.","kahn teel fay BO, ohn suh pro-MEN","When the weather's fine, you go for a walk."],["Quand on est pressé, on se dépêche.","kahn ohn ay press-AY, ohn suh day-PESH","When you're in a hurry, you hurry."]]},{"name":"Ex. 4 — se lever et se coucher","items":[["Vous vous levez à quelle heure, le matin ? — Le matin, nous nous levons à sept heures.","voo voo luh-VAY a kel UR … noo noo luh-VOHN","What time do you get up in the morning?"],["Vous vous couchez à quelle heure, le soir ? — Le soir, nous nous couchons à onze heures.","voo voo koo-SHAY … noo noo koo-SHOHN","What time do you go to bed at night?"],["Vous vous levez à quelle heure, le dimanche ? — Le dimanche, nous nous levons à dix heures.","… luh dee-MAHNSH …","What time do you get up on Sundays?"],["Vous vous couchez à quelle heure, en vacances ? — En vacances, nous nous couchons très tard.","… ahn va-KAHNSS … treh TAR","What time do you go to bed on holiday?"]]},{"name":"Ex. 5 — les verbes et les lieux","cols":"two","items":[["Dans la salle de bains, je me douche, je me lave, je me rase, je me maquille.","dahn lah sal duh BAN, zhuh muh DOOSH, zhuh muh LAHV, zhuh muh RAHZ, zhuh muh ma-KEE","In the bathroom: shower, wash, shave, put on make-up."],["Dans la rue, je me promène, je me dépêche.","dahn lah REW, zhuh muh pro-MEN, zhuh muh day-PESH","In the street: stroll, hurry."],["Dans le jardin, je me repose, je m'amuse.","dahn luh zhar-DAN, zhuh muh ruh-POZ, zhuh ma-MEWZ","In the garden: rest, have fun."],["Dans la chambre, je m'habille, je me déshabille, je me couche, je me parfume.","dahn lah SHAHM-bruh, zhuh ma-BEE, zhuh muh day-za-BEE, zhuh muh KOOSH, zhuh muh par-FEWM","In the bedroom: dress, undress, go to bed, put on perfume."]]},{"name":"Les verbes pronominaux — la liste","cols":"two","items":[["se laver","suh la-VAY","to wash oneself"],["se doucher","suh doo-SHAY","to shower"],["se raser","suh ra-ZAY","to shave"],["se maquiller","suh ma-kee-YAY","to put on make-up"],["se parfumer","suh par-few-MAY","to put on perfume"],["se sécher","suh say-SHAY","to dry oneself"],["s'habiller","sa-bee-YAY","to get dressed"],["se déshabiller","suh day-za-bee-YAY","to get undressed"],["se lever","suh luh-VAY","to get up"],["se coucher","suh koo-SHAY","to go to bed"],["se reposer","suh ruh-po-ZAY","to rest"],["se promener","suh prom-NAY","to go for a walk"],["s'amuser","sa-mew-ZAY","to have fun"],["s'ennuyer","sahn-nwee-YAY","to be bored"],["se dépêcher","suh day-pay-SHAY","to hurry"],["s'appeler","sap-LAY","to be called"]]},{"name":"Le vocabulaire du chapitre","cols":"two","items":[["fatigué / fatiguée","fa-tee-GAY","tired"],["avoir sommeil","a-VWAHR so-MAY","to be sleepy"],["sale","SAL","dirty"],["mouillé / mouillée","moo-YAY","wet"],["pressé / pressée","press-AY","in a hurry"],["tôt","TOH","early"],["tard","TAR","late"],["minuit","mee-NWEE","midnight"],["en semaine","ahn suh-MEN","during the week"],["en vacances","ahn va-KAHNSS","on holiday"],["la salle de bains","lah sal duh BAN","the bathroom"],["la chambre","lah SHAHM-bruh","the bedroom"],["le jardin","luh zhar-DAN","the garden"],["une habitude","ew na-bee-TEWD","a habit"]]},{"name":"Pratiquer le chapitre 9","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"Je ___ lève à sept heures.","a":"me"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Tu ___ appelles comment ?","a":"t'"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Nous ___ couchons tard.","a":"nous"},{"t":"translate","q":"She washes (herself).","a":"Elle se lave."},{"t":"choice","q":"What is your name?","opts":["Comment tu t'appelles ?","Comment tu s'appelles ?"],"a":"Comment tu t'appelles ?"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-recap1","label":"Bilan n° 1","name":"Exercices récapitulatifs · Bilan n° 1","summary":"A short note: this is a review/testing section covering Chapters 1–9, with no new grammar of its own.","art":null,"bookpages":["g028","g029"],"groups":[{"name":"Section de révision","items":[["Bilan n° 1 is a review section (pages 28–29) that mixes exercises across Chapters 1–9 — être and -er verbs, adjective agreement, negation, questions, pronominal verbs — with no new grammar of its own.","bee-LAHN new-may-RO UHN","Review Test No. 1 — a recap, not a new topic"],["Nothing new to summarise here: if you've worked through Grammar → the tense and être/avoir lessons on this site, and Alter Ego Dossiers 0–2, this section is pure practice of material already covered.","…","a pointer rather than new content"]]},{"name":"Bilan 1 — encore","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"Je ___ étudiant.","a":"suis"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Elle est ___. (petit)","a":"petite"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Est-ce que tu ___ ici ?","a":"habites"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Je me ___ à 7 h.","a":"lève"},{"t":"choice","q":"they are big","opts":["ils sont grand","ils sont grands"],"a":"ils sont grands"},{"t":"translate","q":"I am not French.","a":"Je ne suis pas français.","alt":["Je ne suis pas française."]}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-10","label":"Chapitre 10","name":"Un homme, une femme. Un arbre, une route.","summary":"The gender of nouns — masculine and feminine — and how it's shown by the article; the feminine of person-nouns follows the same patterns as adjectives. Original explanation and examples, not transcribed from the book's exercises.","art":null,"bookpages":["g030","g031","g032","g033"],"groups":[{"name":"Le nom a toujours un genre","items":[["Every French noun is grammatically masculine or feminine — for things as much as for people. un arbre (m), une route (f).","uh NAR-bruh, ewn ROOT","a tree, a road — neither is 'neuter'; French has no third gender"],["The article shows the gender: un/le for masculine, une/la for feminine. There's no way to guess a thing's gender from its meaning — it has to be learned with the noun.","UHN/LUH, EWN/LAH","the masculine and feminine article pairs"],["Practical habit: always learn a new noun together with its article — not 'maison' but 'une maison' — so the gender is built in from the start.","ewn may-ZOHN","a house — learned as a unit, not just the word"]]},{"name":"Le féminin des noms de personnes suit le féminin des adjectifs","items":[["The regular pattern: add -e. un étudiant → une étudiante; un ami → une amie.","uh nay-tew-dee-AHN → ewn ay-tew-dee-AHNT","a student (m) → a student (f)"],["-ien → -ienne: un musicien → une musicienne; un Italien → une Italienne.","uhn mew-zee-see-AN → ewn mew-zee-see-EN","a musician (m) → a musician (f)"],["-eur → -euse: un serveur → une serveuse; un danseur → une danseuse.","uhn sair-VUR → ewn sair-VUHZ","a waiter → a waitress"],["-teur → -trice: un acteur → une actrice; un directeur → une directrice.","uh nak-TUR → ewn ak-TREESS","an actor → an actress"],["No change at all: un journaliste → une journaliste; un architecte → une architecte; un artiste → une artiste — words already ending in -e stay exactly the same.","uhn zhoor-na-LEEST","a journalist (m or f, identical)"],["A short list of pairs that don't follow any rule and are simply learned as wholes: un homme / une femme, un monsieur / une dame, un garçon / une fille.","uh NOM / ewn FAM, muh-SYUH / DAM, gar-SOHN / FEE-yuh","man/woman, gentleman/lady, boy/girl"]],"note":"This is exactly the adjective-agreement pattern from the main coursebook's Leçon 1, reapplied to nouns naming people — which makes sense, since a word like <em>étudiant</em> is really 'a person who is studying', functioning as noun and adjective at once."},{"name":"Petite touche d'oreille : la liaison après un","items":[["un ami, un homme — the n of un is pronounced when the next word starts with a vowel, linking the two words together.","u_n a-MEE, u_n OM","a friend, a man — said as one flowing sound"],["Before a consonant, that liaison simply doesn't happen: un livre, un stylo — no linking sound.","uhn LEE-vruh, uhn stee-LO","a book, a pen — no liaison"]]},{"name":"Pratiquer le chapitre 10","quiz":[{"t":"choice","q":"a table","opts":["un table","une table"],"a":"une table"},{"t":"choice","q":"a man","opts":["un homme","une homme"],"a":"un homme"},{"t":"cloze","q":"___ école (feminine)","a":"une"},{"t":"translate","q":"a book and a chair","a":"un livre et une chaise"},{"t":"cloze","q":"___ ami (the noun starts with a vowel, masculine)","a":"un"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-11","label":"Chapitre 11","name":"Des arbres, des fleurs, des oiseaux","summary":"The plural of nouns: the silent -s rule, the -s/-x/-z and -al/-au exceptions, and the liaison that actually carries the 'more than one' meaning aloud.","art":null,"bookpages":["g034","g035"],"groups":[{"name":"Le pluriel des noms : la règle de base","items":[["Add -s to the singular. un arbre → des arbres. une fleur → des fleurs. un garçon → des garçons.","day ZAR-bruh, day FLUR, day gar-SOHN","trees, flowers, boys"],["That final -s is silent — you cannot hear the plural on the noun itself. What you actually hear is the article changing: un/une → des.","day","the plural article — the real audible signal of 'more than one'"]]},{"name":"Les cas particuliers du pluriel","items":[["Nouns already ending in -s, -x or -z: no change at all. un pays → des pays. un choix → des choix. un nez → des nez.","day pay-EE, day SHWAH, day NAY","countries, choices, noses — identical in singular and plural"],["Nouns ending in -al or -au: the ending becomes -aux. un journal → des journaux. un animal → des animaux. un gâteau → des gâteaux.","day zhoor-NO, day za-nee-MO, day ga-TO","newspapers, animals, cakes"],["A handful of very common nouns are simply irregular and learned individually: un œil → des yeux (a completely different word), monsieur → messieurs, madame → mesdames.","day ZYUH, may-SYUH, may-DAM","eyes, gentlemen, ladies"]]},{"name":"La liaison au pluriel : le son [z]","items":[["des amis, des hommes — before a vowel, the s of des is pronounced as a z, linking the words.","day_z a-MEE, day_z OM","friends, men — the z-sound carries across"],["This is the plural counterpart to the un/une liaison from Chapter 10 — in both cases it's the article's hidden consonant, not anything on the noun, that you actually hear.","…","the same mechanism, now on des rather than un"]]},{"name":"Pratiquer le chapitre 11","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"un chat → des ___","a":"chats"},{"t":"cloze","q":"un journal → des ___","a":"journaux"},{"t":"choice","q":"some animals (animal)","opts":["des animals","des animaux"],"a":"des animaux"},{"t":"translate","q":"apples","a":"des pommes"},{"t":"cloze","q":"une femme → des ___","a":"femmes"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-12","label":"Chapitre 12","name":"Une tour, un pont, des bateaux","summary":"Indefinite vs definite articles side by side — non-specific/category vs specific/unique, plus the definite article's use for generalities — with a practical test for telling them apart.","art":null,"bookpages":["g036","g037"],"groups":[{"name":"Article indéfini : une chose parmi d'autres","items":[["un / une / des point to something non-specific — one example from a category, or a simple quantity. un pont (some bridge or other, not a particular one) — deux enfants, des jouets (some toys, unspecified).","uhn POHN … day zhoo-AY","a bridge (any bridge) — toys (some, unspecified)"],["Un/une can also simply mean the number 'one': un homme, une femme = one man, one woman.","uh NOM, ewn FAM","one man, one woman — the numeral sense"]]},{"name":"Article défini : une chose précise, ou une généralité","items":[["le / la / les point to something specific and already identified — a particular, unique thing. le Pont-Neuf (that specific bridge, the one with that name) — la femme de Paul (a specific woman: Paul's).","luh pohn-NUF … lah fam duh POL","the Pont-Neuf (this particular bridge) — Paul's wife (a specific person)"],["The definite article also serves for generalities — speaking about a whole category as a concept. l'homme (= mankind in general) — la musique, le sport, le cinéma (these things as categories, not one particular instance).","LOM, lah mew-ZEEK, luh SPOR, luh see-nay-MAH","man(kind), music, sport, cinema — spoken of as whole categories"],["The test that separates the two: could you replace it with 'a certain, some' (→ indefinite) or with 'that particular one / the whole category' (→ definite)? J'ai vu un chat (some cat) vs. J'ai vu le chat du voisin (a specific, identified cat).","zhay vew uh SHAH … luh shah dew vwa-ZAN","I saw a cat (some cat) vs. I saw the neighbour's cat (a specific one)"]]},{"name":"Les deux tableaux, côte à côte","items":[["Indéfini — singulier masc. un, singulier fém. une, pluriel (les deux genres) des.","UHN, EWN, DAY","a/an (m), a/an (f), some (either gender)"],["Défini — singulier masc. le (l' devant voyelle), singulier fém. la (l' devant voyelle), pluriel (les deux genres) les.","LUH (L'), LAH (L'), LAY","the (m), the (f), the (plural) — l' replaces le/la before a vowel sound"]],"note":"A learner's rule of thumb that covers most everyday cases: the first time you mention something, it's usually indefinite (un/une/des); once it's been named and everyone knows which one you mean, it becomes definite (le/la/les). <em>J'ai un chat. Le chat s'appelle Milo.</em> — 'I have a cat. The cat is called Milo.'"},{"name":"Pratiquer le chapitre 12","quiz":[{"t":"choice","q":"a specific tower you both see","opts":["une tour","la tour"],"a":"la tour"},{"t":"choice","q":"one tower, any tower","opts":["une tour","la tour"],"a":"une tour"},{"t":"cloze","q":"J'aime ___ musique.","a":"la"},{"t":"translate","q":"I am buying a book.","a":"J'achète un livre."},{"t":"cloze","q":"___ soleil brille.","a":"Le"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-13","label":"Chapitre 13","name":"Je visite le Louvre. Je suis au Louvre.","summary":"The contracted articles au/aux/du/des in full: only le and les ever contract, with à or de; la and l' never change.","art":null,"bookpages":["g038","g039"],"groups":[{"name":"À + article défini : deux contractions, deux cas où rien ne change","items":[["à + le = au. Je vais au Louvre (à + le Louvre).","zhuh vay oh LOO-vruh","I'm going to the Louvre — au is compulsory; 'à le Louvre' does not exist"],["à + les = aux. Je vais aux Invalides (à + les Invalides).","zhuh vay oh zan-va-LEED","I'm going to Les Invalides"],["à + la stays à la — no contraction. Je vais à la Bastille.","zhuh vay a lah bas-TEE-yuh","I'm going to the Bastille — nothing changes before la"],["à + l' stays à l' — no contraction. Je vais à l'Opéra.","zhuh vay a lo-pay-RAH","I'm going to the Opera — nothing changes before l'"]]},{"name":"De + article défini : les mêmes deux contractions","items":[["de + le = du. les chaussures du père (de + le père).","lay sho-SEWR dew PAIR","the father's shoes"],["de + les = des. les chaussures des Martiens (de + les Martiens).","lay sho-SEWR day mar-see-AN","the Martians' shoes"],["de + la stays de la — no contraction. les chaussures de la mère.","lay sho-SEWR duh lah MAIR","the mother's shoes"],["de + l' stays de l' — no contraction. les chaussures de l'enfant.","lay sho-SEWR duh lahn-FAHN","the child's shoes"]],"note":"Only <strong>le</strong> and <strong>les</strong> ever contract, with either à or de — because le and les are the only definite articles that start with a consonant sound the following word can 'merge' into. la and l' are left untouched every time, in both patterns. This is the same rule the main coursebook introduces for du/de la/de l'/des with places in town — Chapter 13 is really the general statement behind that specific case."},{"name":"Pratiquer le chapitre 13","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"Je vais ___ musée.","a":"au"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Elle vient ___ Italie.","a":"d'"},{"t":"choice","q":"at the café","opts":["à le café","au café"],"a":"au café"},{"t":"translate","q":"I come back from the office.","a":"Je reviens du bureau."},{"t":"cloze","q":"un souvenir ___ Louvre","a":"du"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-14","label":"Chapitre 14","name":"Mon père, ton père, son père","summary":"Possessive adjectives in full, including the nous/vous/ils forms often left out of A1 coverage, the agreement-with-the-thing-owned rule, and the mon/ton/son-before-a-vowel exception.","art":null,"bookpages":["g040","g041"],"groups":[{"name":"L'adjectif possessif s'accorde avec la chose possédée, pas avec le possesseur","items":[["This is the rule that trips up most learners: French possessives agree with the THING owned, not the person who owns it. son père can mean 'his father' or 'her father' — you cannot tell which from the word alone.","sohn PAIR","his/her father — son here because père is masculine, whoever the owner is"],["sa mère likewise means 'his mother' or 'her mother' — sa because mère is feminine, regardless of the owner's own gender.","sa MAIR","his/her mother"],["Context, not the possessive, tells you who owns it: Paul aime sa mère (Paul loves his mother) — Marie aime sa mère (Marie loves her mother). Identical possessive, different owner.","pol em sa MAIR … ma-REE em sa MAIR","Paul loves his mother — Marie loves her mother"]]},{"name":"Le tableau complet des possessifs","items":[["Je → mon père, ma mère, mes parents","mohn PAIR, ma MAIR, may pa-RAHN","my father, my mother, my parents"],["Tu → ton père, ta mère, tes parents","tohn PAIR, ta MAIR, tay pa-RAHN","your father, your mother, your parents (tu-form)"],["Il/Elle → son père, sa mère, ses parents","sohn PAIR, sa MAIR, say pa-RAHN","his/her father, mother, parents"],["Nous → notre père, notre mère, nos parents","NOT-ruh PAIR, NOT-ruh MAIR, no pa-RAHN","our father, our mother, our parents"],["Vous → votre père, votre mère, vos parents","VOT-ruh PAIR, VOT-ruh MAIR, vo pa-RAHN","your father, your mother, your parents (vous-form)"],["Ils/Elles → leur père, leur mère, leurs parents","lur PAIR, lur MAIR, lur pa-RAHN","their father, their mother, their parents"]],"note":"Notice the shape of the whole system: singular owners (je/tu/il) give three different forms depending on the noun's gender and number (mon/ma/mes), but plural owners (nous/vous/ils) give only two — one shared form for masculine and feminine singular (notre, votre), and a separate plural (nos, vos). <strong>Leur/leurs</strong> agrees only in number, exactly like nos/vos.","cols":"two"},{"name":"Ma, ta, sa deviennent mon, ton, son devant une voyelle","items":[["The feminine forms ma, ta, sa are replaced by the masculine mon, ton, son whenever the next word starts with a vowel sound — purely for pronunciation, so two vowels don't collide.","MOHN, TOHN, SOHN","the masculine forms, borrowed here for sound reasons only"],["mon amie (not ma amie) — the noun amie is feminine, but mon is used because of the vowel.","moh na-MEE","my (female) friend — mon, even though amie is feminine"],["ton erreur (not ta erreur), son école (not sa école) — same logic each time.","toh nay-RUR, soh nay-KOL","your mistake, his/her school"]],"note":"This is a pronunciation rule dressed up as a grammar rule — French avoids putting two vowel sounds back to back where it can. The noun's actual gender hasn't changed; only the spoken form of the possessive has, to keep the liaison smooth."},{"name":"Pratiquer le chapitre 14","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"___ père (my, masculine)","a":"mon"},{"t":"cloze","q":"___ mère (my)","a":"ma"},{"t":"cloze","q":"___ amis (my)","a":"mes"},{"t":"choice","q":"her book (the book is masculine)","opts":["sa livre","son livre"],"a":"son livre"},{"t":"translate","q":"our house","a":"notre maison"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-15","label":"Chapitre 15","name":"Ce, cette, ces","summary":"Demonstrative adjectives: this / that / these, agreeing with the noun.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"La règle","note":"Put <strong>ce</strong> before a masculine noun, <strong>cet</strong> before a masculine noun starting with a vowel or mute h, <strong>cette</strong> before a feminine noun, <strong>ces</strong> before any plural. Add <strong>-ci</strong> or <strong>-là</strong> only when you must point: this one here, that one there.","items":[["ce livre","suh leEVR","this / that book"],["cet homme","set ohnm","this / that man"],["cet hôtel","set ohtUHL","this / that hotel"],["cette femme","set faHNM","this / that woman"],["cette école","set aykOHL","this / that school"],["ces livres","say leEVR","these / those books"],["ces femmes","say faHNM","these / those women"],["ce film-ci ou ce film-là ?","suh feelm-SEE oo suh feelm-LAH","this film or that film?"],["Je préfère cette voiture.","zhuh prayfEHR set vwahtEWR","I prefer this car."],["Cet appartement est calme.","set ahppahrtuhmaHNT eh kaHLM","This flat is quiet."]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"___ livre est à moi.","a":"Ce","alt":["ce"]},{"t":"cloze","q":"___ ami habite à Lyon.","a":"Cet","alt":["cet"]},{"t":"cloze","q":"___ maison est grande.","a":"Cette","alt":["cette"]},{"t":"cloze","q":"___ enfants sont français.","a":"Ces","alt":["ces"]},{"t":"choice","q":"Masculine noun with a vowel.","opts":["ce ami","cet ami","cette ami"],"a":"cet ami"},{"t":"translate","q":"I prefer this café.","a":"Je préfère ce café.","alt":["Je préfère ce café-ci."]}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-16","label":"Chapitre 16","name":"J'ai une voiture","summary":"Avoir plus a noun, and where a short adjective sits.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Avoir + nom","note":"Possession, features and a lot of everyday nouns use <strong>avoir</strong>, not être. Most short adjectives go <strong>before</strong> the noun (petit, grand, bon, mauvais, beau, joli, jeune, vieux, nouveau). Most others go after (rouge, français, intéressant).","items":[["J'ai une voiture.","zhay ewn vwahtEWR","I have a car."],["Tu as un vélo ?","tew ah uhn vayLOH","Do you have a bike?"],["Elle a une petite maison.","ell ah ewn puh-TEET mehzOHN","She has a small house."],["Il a un grand appartement.","eel ah uhn grahn ahppahrtuhmaHNT","He has a large flat."],["Nous avons un chat noir.","noo ah-VOHN uhn shah nwAHR","We have a black cat."],["un bon café","uhn bohn kahFAY","a good coffee"],["une voiture rouge","ewn vwahtEWR roOZH","a red car"],["un vieux livre","uhn veEUH leEVR","an old book"],["une jeune femme","ewn zhUHN faHNM","a young woman"],["Ils ont des amis italiens.","eel ohn day ahMEE eetahlyANS","They have Italian friends."]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"J'___ une voiture bleue.","a":"ai"},{"t":"choice","q":"Where does the adjective go?","opts":["une rouge voiture","une voiture rouge"],"a":"une voiture rouge"},{"t":"choice","q":"Short adjective before the noun.","opts":["une petite maison","une maison petite"],"a":"une petite maison"},{"t":"translate","q":"She has a black cat.","a":"Elle a un chat noir."},{"t":"cloze","q":"Nous ___ un petit appartement.","a":"avons"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-17","label":"Chapitre 17","name":"Les yeux noirs, trois ans","summary":"Describing someone, and saying an age with avoir.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Le portrait","note":"Hair, eyes and other features: <strong>avoir</strong> + article + noun + adjective. Age is also <strong>avoir</strong>: j'ai vingt ans. Never <em>je suis vingt ans</em>.","items":[["Elle a les yeux bleus.","ell ah lay eeuh bluh","She has blue eyes."],["Il a les cheveux noirs.","eel ah lay shuhVUH nwaHRS","He has black hair."],["Tu as les cheveux longs.","tew ah lay shuhVUH lohNGS","You have long hair."],["J'ai les yeux marron.","zhay lay eeuh mahrrOHN","I have brown eyes."],["J'ai vingt ans.","zhay vaNGT ahns","I am twenty."],["Quel âge as-tu ?","kuhl ahzh ahs-TEW","How old are you?"],["Elle a trente-deux ans.","ell ah trahntuh-DUH ahns","She is thirty-two."],["Le bébé a six mois.","luh bayBAY ah see mwah","The baby is six months old."],["Il est grand et mince.","eel eh grahn ay mans","He is tall and slim."],["Elle est petite et brune.","ell eh puh-TEET ay brUHN","She is short and dark-haired."]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"Elle a ___ yeux verts.","a":"les"},{"t":"cloze","q":"J'ai vingt ___.","a":"ans"},{"t":"choice","q":"How old is he? He is 10.","opts":["Il est dix ans.","Il a dix ans."],"a":"Il a dix ans."},{"t":"translate","q":"She has long hair.","a":"Elle a les cheveux longs."},{"t":"cloze","q":"Quel ___ as-tu ?","a":"âge"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-18","label":"Chapitre 18","name":"Il a mal à la tête","summary":"Avoir expressions: hunger, thirst, heat, cold, fear, sleep, being right, and pain.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Les expressions avec avoir","note":"These ideas use <strong>avoir</strong> in French and <em>be</em> in English. Pain is <strong>avoir mal à</strong> + the definite article: j'ai mal à la tête, j'ai mal aux dents.","items":[["J'ai faim.","zhay fan","I am hungry."],["Tu as soif ?","tew ah swAHF","Are you thirsty?"],["Il a chaud.","eel ah shoh","He is hot."],["Elle a froid.","ell ah frWAH","She is cold."],["Nous avons peur.","noo ah-VOHN puhr","We are afraid."],["J'ai sommeil.","zhay sohnmEHL","I am sleepy."],["Tu as raison.","tew ah rehzOHN","You are right."],["Il a tort.","eel ah toHRT","He is wrong."],["J'ai mal à la tête.","zhay mahl ah lah teht","I have a headache."],["Elle a mal au dos.","ell ah mahl oh doh","Her back hurts."],["Ils ont mal aux pieds.","eel ohn mahl oh peeuHDS","Their feet hurt."]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"J'ai ___. Je veux un sandwich.","a":"faim"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Il a mal ___ tête.","a":"à la","hint":"à + la"},{"t":"choice","q":"I am cold.","opts":["Je suis froid.","J'ai froid."],"a":"J'ai froid."},{"t":"translate","q":"She is thirsty.","a":"Elle a soif."},{"t":"cloze","q":"Vous avez ___. C'est vrai.","a":"raison"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-19","label":"Chapitre 19","name":"J'ai, tu as, il a","summary":"The full present of avoir, and questions with it.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Le verbe avoir","note":"Avoir is irregular. In a question with inversion, the <strong>-t-</strong> appears between a and il/elle: a-t-il, a-t-elle.","items":[["j'ai","zhay","I have"],["tu as","tew ah","you have"],["il a / elle a","eel ah / ell ah","he has / she has"],["nous avons","noo ah-VOHN","we have"],["vous avez","voo ah-VAY","you have"],["ils ont / elles ont","eel ohn / ell ohn","they have"],["Est-ce que tu as un frère ?","ess-kuh tew ah uhn frEHR","Do you have a brother?"],["A-t-elle une voiture ?","ah-t-UHL ewn vwahtEWR","Does she have a car?"],["Vous avez l'heure ?","voo ah-VAY luhr","Do you have the time?"],["Ils ont deux enfants.","eel ohn duh ahnfahNTS","They have two children."]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"Nous ___ un chien.","a":"avons"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Vous ___ raison.","a":"avez"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Elles ___ faim.","a":"ont"},{"t":"choice","q":"Does he have a bike?","opts":["A-t-il un vélo ?","A-il un vélo ?","Est-il un vélo ?"],"a":"A-t-il un vélo ?"},{"t":"translate","q":"I have two sisters.","a":"J'ai deux sœurs."}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-20","label":"Chapitre 20","name":"Je n'ai pas de chat","summary":"Negation: pas de instead of pas un / pas le, with the main exceptions.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Pas de","note":"After a negative, <strong>un, une, des</strong> and the partitive <strong>du, de la</strong> become <strong>de</strong> (d' before a vowel). The definite article stays when you mean that particular thing: je n'aime pas le café. <strong>Être</strong> keeps the article: ce n'est pas un problème.","items":[["J'ai un chat. → Je n'ai pas de chat.","zhay uhn shah → zhuh nay pah duh shah","I have a cat. → I don't have a cat."],["Il a une voiture. → Il n'a pas de voiture.","eel ah ewn vwahtEWR → eel nah pah duh vwahtEWR","He doesn't have a car."],["Je mange de la viande. → Je ne mange pas de viande.","zhuh mahNZH duh lah veeaHND → zhuh nuh mahNZH pah duh veeaHND","I don't eat meat."],["Tu veux du café ? — Non, je ne veux pas de café.","tew vuh dew kahFAY — nohn zhuh nuh vuh pah duh kahFAY","No coffee for me."],["Je n'ai pas d'argent.","zhuh nay pah dahRZH","I don't have any money."],["Elle n'aime pas le café.","ell nan pah luh kahFAY","She doesn't like coffee. (in general)"],["Ce n'est pas une bonne idée.","suh neh pah ewn boHNN eedaYUH","That is not a good idea."],["Il n'y a pas de lait.","eel nee ah pah duh leh","There isn't any milk."]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"Je n'ai pas ___ frère.","a":"de"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Elle ne mange pas ___ viande.","a":"de"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Je n'ai pas ___ argent.","a":"d'","alt":["d'"]},{"t":"choice","q":"She doesn't like coffee in general.","opts":["Elle n'aime pas de café.","Elle n'aime pas le café."],"a":"Elle n'aime pas le café."},{"t":"translate","q":"There isn't a problem.","a":"Il n'y a pas de problème.","alt":["Ce n'est pas un problème."]}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-recap2","label":"Bilan n° 2","name":"Être, avoir, le nom","summary":"Mixed review of chapters 10 to 20: gender, articles, avoir, age, pain, pas de.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Bilan 2","quiz":[{"t":"choice","q":"Feminine article.","opts":["un table","une table"],"a":"une table"},{"t":"cloze","q":"J'___ vingt ans.","a":"ai"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Elle a mal ___ gorge.","a":"à la"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Nous n'avons pas ___ voiture.","a":"de"},{"t":"choice","q":"This (feminine).","opts":["ce maison","cette maison"],"a":"cette maison"},{"t":"translate","q":"I am hungry and I have a headache.","a":"J'ai faim et j'ai mal à la tête."},{"t":"cloze","q":"Ils ___ les cheveux courts.","a":"ont"},{"t":"choice","q":"Adjective after the noun.","opts":["une bleue voiture","une voiture bleue"],"a":"une voiture bleue"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-21","label":"Chapitre 21","name":"À, de, chez, près de, loin de","summary":"The small prepositions that locate people and places.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Où ?","note":"<strong>chez</strong> + person = at that person's home. <strong>à</strong> is the general 'at / to'. <strong>de</strong> is 'from' or 'of'. près de = near, loin de = far from.","items":[["Je vais à l'école.","zhuh veh ah laykOHL","I go to school."],["Elle est à la maison.","ell eh ah lah mehzOHN","She is at home."],["On dîne chez Paul.","ohn dan shay pohl","We're having dinner at Paul's."],["Tu habites chez tes parents ?","tew ahbEET shay tay pahrahNTS","Do you live at your parents'?"],["J'habite près de la gare.","zhah-BEET prEHS duh lah gahr","I live near the station."],["C'est loin de Paris.","seh lwAHN duh pah-REE","It's far from Paris."],["Je viens de Lyon.","zhuh vyANS duh leeOHN","I come from Lyon."],["le livre de Marie","luh leEVR duh mahreEUH","Marie's book"],["Il rentre de chez le médecin.","eel rahNTR duh shay luh mayduhSAN","He's coming back from the doctor's."]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"On mange ___ mes parents ce soir.","a":"chez"},{"t":"cloze","q":"J'habite ___ de la poste.","a":"près"},{"t":"cloze","q":"C'est ___ de la mer.","a":"loin"},{"t":"choice","q":"at the doctor's","opts":["à le médecin","chez le médecin"],"a":"chez le médecin"},{"t":"translate","q":"I come from Lille.","a":"Je viens de Lille."}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-22","label":"Chapitre 22","name":"En France, au Japon","summary":"Countries and cities: en, au, aux, à.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Les pays","note":"Feminine countries (usually ending in e): <strong>en</strong> France, en Chine. Masculine: <strong>au</strong> Japon, au Canada. Plural: <strong>aux</strong> États-Unis. Cities: <strong>à</strong> Paris, à Londres. Coming from uses de / du / des: de France, du Japon, des États-Unis.","items":[["J'habite en France.","zhah-BEET ahn frahns","I live in France."],["Elle part au Japon.","ell paHRT oh zhahpOHN","She is leaving for Japan."],["Ils vivent aux États-Unis.","eel veev oh aytahts-ewNEE","They live in the United States."],["Nous allons au Portugal.","noo ahloHNS oh pohrtewgAHL","We are going to Portugal."],["Tu es en Italie ?","tew eh ahn eetahleEUH","Are you in Italy?"],["Je travaille à Paris.","zhuh trahvEHL ah pah-REE","I work in Paris."],["Il arrive de Madrid.","eel ahrrEEV duh mahdREE","He arrives from Madrid."],["Elle vient du Maroc.","ell vee dew mahrOHS","She comes from Morocco."],["au Mexique, au Cambodge","oh muhkseeKUH oh kahnbohDZH","Mexico, Cambodia (masculine exceptions in -e)"],["en Iran, en Israël","ahn eerAHN ahn eesrahEHL","Iran, Israel (feminine, no e)"]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"J'habite ___ France.","a":"en"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Il va ___ Canada.","a":"au"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Nous sommes ___ Paris.","a":"à"},{"t":"choice","q":"in the United States","opts":["en États-Unis","aux États-Unis","au États-Unis"],"a":"aux États-Unis"},{"t":"translate","q":"She comes from Japan.","a":"Elle vient du Japon."}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-23","label":"Chapitre 23","name":"Dans, sur, sous, devant, derrière","summary":"Prepositions of place you can point at.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"La position","note":"dans = inside, sur = on, sous = under, devant = in front of, derrière = behind, entre = between, à côté de = next to, en face de = opposite.","items":[["Le chat est dans la boîte.","luh shah eh dahn lah bwAHT","The cat is in the box."],["Les clés sont sur la table.","lay klAYS sohn sewr lah taHBL","The keys are on the table."],["Le sac est sous la chaise.","luh sahs eh soo lah shEHS","The bag is under the chair."],["La voiture est devant la maison.","lah vwahtEWR eh duhvaHNT lah mehzOHN","The car is in front of the house."],["Le jardin est derrière.","luh zhahrDAN eh duhrreeEHR","The garden is behind."],["J'habite entre la poste et la banque.","zhah-BEET ahNTR lah poHST ay lah bahnKUH","I live between the post office and the bank."],["Le café est à côté de la gare.","luh kahFAY eh ah kohTAY duh lah gahr","The café is next to the station."],["L'arrêt est en face de l'école.","lahrrEHT eh ahn fahs duh laykOHL","The stop is opposite the school."]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"Les clés sont ___ la table.","a":"sur"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Le chat dort ___ le lit.","a":"sous"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Attends ___ la porte.","a":"devant"},{"t":"choice","q":"next to the bank","opts":["à côté de la banque","en face la banque"],"a":"à côté de la banque"},{"t":"translate","q":"The book is in the bag.","a":"Le livre est dans le sac."}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-24","label":"Chapitre 24","name":"Il y a","summary":"There is / there are, and the negative il n'y a pas de.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Il y a","note":"<strong>Il y a</strong> never changes for plural. The question is <strong>Est-ce qu'il y a… ?</strong> or <strong>Y a-t-il… ?</strong> Negative: <strong>il n'y a pas de</strong> + noun.","items":[["Il y a un parc près d'ici.","eel ee ah uhn paHRS prEHS dee-SEE","There is a park nearby."],["Il y a des étudiants dans la classe.","eel ee ah day aytewdeeahNTS dahn lah klaHSS","There are students in the class."],["Est-ce qu'il y a un médecin ?","uhsT-S keel ee ah uhn mayduhSAN","Is there a doctor?"],["Y a-t-il du pain ?","ee ah-t-EEL dew pan","Is there any bread?"],["Il n'y a pas de lait.","eel nee ah pah duh leh","There is no milk."],["Il n'y a personne.","eel nee ah puhrsoHNN","There is nobody."],["Qu'est-ce qu'il y a dans ton sac ?","kuhsT-S keel ee ah dahn tohn sahs","What is in your bag?"],["Il y a trois chambres.","eel ee ah trWAH shahNBR","There are three bedrooms."]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"___ un café en face.","a":"Il y a"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Il n'y a pas ___ sucre.","a":"de"},{"t":"choice","q":"Are there any tickets?","opts":["Est-ce qu'il y a des billets ?","Est-ce que il y a des billets ?"],"a":"Est-ce qu'il y a des billets ?"},{"t":"translate","q":"There is no problem.","a":"Il n'y a pas de problème."},{"t":"cloze","q":"Y ___-t-il une pharmacie ?","a":"a"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-25","label":"Chapitre 25","name":"Qui est-ce ? Qu'est-ce que c'est ?","summary":"Asking who and what, with c'est.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Qui et quoi","note":"<strong>Qui est-ce ?</strong> asks about a person. <strong>Qu'est-ce que c'est ?</strong> asks about a thing. You answer with <strong>c'est</strong> + noun. <strong>Qui</strong> is also the subject of a verb: qui parle ?","items":[["Qui est-ce ?","kee uhsT-S","Who is it?"],["C'est mon frère.","seh mohn frEHR","It's my brother."],["C'est Marie.","seh mahreEUH","It's Marie."],["Qu'est-ce que c'est ?","kess-kuh seh","What is it?"],["C'est un livre.","seh uhn leEVR","It's a book."],["Qui parle ?","kee paHRL","Who is speaking?"],["C'est moi.","seh mwah","It's me."],["Qu'est-ce que tu fais ?","kess-kuh tew feh","What are you doing?"],["Qui tu invites ?","kee tew anvEET","Who are you inviting?"]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"choice","q":"What is it?","opts":["Qui est-ce ?","Qu'est-ce que c'est ?"],"a":"Qu'est-ce que c'est ?"},{"t":"cloze","q":"___ est-ce ? — C'est Paul.","a":"Qui"},{"t":"translate","q":"It's my sister.","a":"C'est ma sœur."},{"t":"cloze","q":"Qu'est-ce que tu ___ ?","a":"fais","hint":"faire"},{"t":"choice","q":"It's me.","opts":["C'est je.","C'est moi."],"a":"C'est moi."}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-26","label":"Chapitre 26","name":"C'est ou il est","summary":"When to use c'est and when to use il est / elle est.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Deux façons de dire","note":"<strong>C'est</strong> + article + noun: c'est un médecin, c'est Marie, c'est un bon film. <strong>Il est / elle est</strong> + adjective with no article, or + profession with no article: il est médecin, elle est grande, il est français. Don't say <em>il est un médecin</em> or <em>c'est médecin</em>.","items":[["C'est un professeur.","seh uhn prohfuhssUHR","He's a teacher. (pointing someone out)"],["Il est professeur.","eel eh prohfuhssUHR","He is a teacher. (his job)"],["C'est une bonne idée.","seh ewn boHNN eedaYUH","That's a good idea."],["Elle est intelligente.","ell eh antuhleezhaHNT","She is intelligent."],["C'est Paul. Il est sympa.","seh pohl eel eh sanPAH","That's Paul. He's nice."],["Il est français. C'est un ami.","eel eh frahn-SEH seh uhn ahMEE","He's French. He's a friend."],["C'est cher.","seh shUHR","That's expensive. (a thing already known)"],["Elle est médecin à Lyon.","ell eh mayduhSAN ah leeOHN","She's a doctor in Lyon."]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"choice","q":"Her job, no article.","opts":["Elle est médecin.","Elle est une médecin."],"a":"Elle est médecin."},{"t":"choice","q":"Pointing at a profession with an article.","opts":["C'est un médecin.","Il est un médecin."],"a":"C'est un médecin."},{"t":"cloze","q":"___ est grand et sportif.","a":"Il"},{"t":"translate","q":"That's my brother. He's nice.","a":"C'est mon frère. Il est sympa."},{"t":"cloze","q":"___ une bonne idée.","a":"C'est"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-27","label":"Chapitre 27","name":"C'est beau !","summary":"Reacting to a thing with c'est + adjective.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Un commentaire","note":"Once the thing is known, comment with <strong>c'est</strong> + masculine singular adjective: c'est beau, c'est bon, c'est cher, c'est intéressant. The adjective does not change for a feminine noun you are pointing at.","items":[["Regarde cette maison. C'est beau !","ruhgaHRD set mehzOHN seh boh","Look at that house. It's beautiful!"],["Ce gâteau, c'est bon.","suh gahTOH seh bohn","This cake is good."],["C'est trop cher.","seh troh shUHR","That's too expensive."],["C'est nul.","seh newl","That's rubbish."],["C'est génial !","seh zhayneeAHL","That's brilliant!"],["C'est difficile.","seh deeffeesEEL","It's difficult."],["C'est facile.","seh fahsEEL","It's easy."],["C'est possible ?","seh pohsseEBL","Is that possible?"],["Ce n'est pas grave.","suh neh pah grAHV","It doesn't matter."]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"Cette robe, ___ beau !","a":"c'est"},{"t":"choice","q":"The adjective stays masculine.","opts":["C'est belle.","C'est beau."],"a":"C'est beau."},{"t":"translate","q":"That's too expensive.","a":"C'est trop cher."},{"t":"cloze","q":"Ce n'est pas ___.","a":"grave","hint":"it doesn't matter"},{"t":"choice","q":"It's easy.","opts":["C'est facile.","Il est facile."],"a":"C'est facile."}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-recap3","label":"Bilan n° 3","name":"Le lieu, c'est, il y a","summary":"Review of prepositions, countries, il y a, and c'est / il est.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Bilan 3","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"J'habite ___ Paris.","a":"à"},{"t":"choice","q":"in Japan","opts":["en Japon","au Japon"],"a":"au Japon"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Le chat est ___ la table.","a":"sous","hint":"under"},{"t":"cloze","q":"___ un marché le samedi.","a":"Il y a"},{"t":"choice","q":"She is a lawyer.","opts":["Elle est avocate.","Elle est une avocate."],"a":"Elle est avocate."},{"t":"translate","q":"There is no bread.","a":"Il n'y a pas de pain."},{"t":"cloze","q":"On dîne ___ Léa.","a":"chez"},{"t":"translate","q":"That's a good idea.","a":"C'est une bonne idée."}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-28","label":"Chapitre 28","name":"Les nombres et la date","summary":"Numbers you use to count, to rank, and to say the date.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Compter, classer, dater","note":"Cardinal numbers count. Ordinals rank, and they are regular after premier / première: deuxième, troisième… The date is <strong>le</strong> + cardinal (not ordinal), except the first: le 1<sup>er</sup> mai, le 2 mai. Months have no capital.","items":[["zéro, un, deux, trois, quatre, cinq","zayROH uhn duh trWAH kaHTR sanq","0 to 5"],["dix, vingt, trente, quarante, cinquante","dee vaNGT traHNT kahraHNT sankaHNT","10, 20, 30, 40, 50"],["soixante-dix, quatre-vingts, quatre-vingt-dix","swahksahntuh-DEE kahtruh-vanGTS kahtruh-vangt-DEE","70, 80, 90"],["cent, mille","s my","100, 1000"],["le premier étage","luh pruhmeeUHR aytaHZH","the first floor"],["la deuxième rue","lah duhkseeEHM reWUH","the second street"],["le 1er janvier","luh 1uhr zhahnveeUHR","1 January"],["le 14 juillet","luh 14 zhEWY","14 July"],["Nous sommes le 4 novembre.","noo sum luh 4 nohvahNBR","Today is 4 November."],["en 2026","ahn 2026","in 2026"]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"70 s'écrit ___.","a":"soixante-dix"},{"t":"cloze","q":"80 s'écrit quatre-___.","a":"vingts","hint":"with an s when nothing follows"},{"t":"choice","q":"2 May","opts":["le 2ème mai","le 2 mai"],"a":"le 2 mai"},{"t":"cloze","q":"le ___ janvier","a":"1er","alt":["premier"]},{"t":"translate","q":"Today is 8 March.","a":"Nous sommes le 8 mars.","alt":["Nous sommes le huit mars."]}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-29","label":"Chapitre 29","name":"L'heure","summary":"Telling the time.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Quelle heure est-il ?","note":"Official time uses <strong>heure(s)</strong>. Midi and minuit stand alone. et quart, et demie, moins le quart. In the afternoon, add de l'après-midi, or use the 24-hour clock, which is what timetables use.","items":[["Quelle heure est-il ?","kuhl uhr uhst-EEL","What time is it?"],["Il est une heure.","eel eh ewn uhr","It's one o'clock."],["Il est deux heures.","eel eh duh uhr","It's two o'clock."],["Il est trois heures et quart.","eel eh trWAH uhr ay kaHRT","It's quarter past three."],["Il est quatre heures et demie.","eel eh kaHTR uhr ay duhmeEUH","It's half past four."],["Il est cinq heures moins le quart.","eel eh sanq uhr mwaHNS luh kaHRT","It's quarter to five."],["Il est midi. Il est minuit.","eel eh meeDEE eel eh meeneWEE","It's noon. It's midnight."],["à huit heures du matin","ah ewee uhr dew mahTAN","at eight in the morning"],["Le train part à 18 h 40.","luh tran paHRT ah 18 40","The train leaves at 18:40."],["vers dix heures","vehr dee uhr","around ten"]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"Il est midi et ___.","a":"demi","alt":["demie"],"hint":"noon + 30 min — midi takes demi"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Il est deux heures et ___.","a":"demie"},{"t":"choice","q":"It's one o'clock.","opts":["Il est une heures.","Il est une heure."],"a":"Il est une heure."},{"t":"translate","q":"What time is it?","a":"Quelle heure est-il ?"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Le cours est à neuf ___ .","a":"heures"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-30","label":"Chapitre 30","name":"La météo, les mois, les saisons","summary":"Weather with faire, être and il y a, plus months and seasons.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Quel temps fait-il ?","note":"Most weather is <strong>il fait</strong> + adjective. Rain, snow and wind use <strong>il y a</strong> or a verb: il pleut, il neige. Seasons: au printemps, en été, en automne, en hiver. Months: en janvier.","items":[["Il fait beau.","eel feh boh","The weather is nice."],["Il fait mauvais.","eel feh mohVEH","The weather is bad."],["Il fait chaud. Il fait froid.","eel feh shoh eel feh frWAH","It's hot. It's cold."],["Il y a du soleil. Il y a du vent.","eel ee ah dew sohlEHL eel ee ah dew v","It's sunny. It's windy."],["Il pleut. Il neige.","eel pluh eel neHZH","It's raining. It's snowing."],["en janvier, en février, en mars","ahn zhahnveeUHR ahn fayvreeUHR ahn maHRS","in January, February, March"],["en avril, en mai, en juin","ahn ahvrEEL ahn meh ahn zheWAN","in April, May, June"],["en juillet, en août, en septembre","ahn zhEWY ahn ahoo ahn suhptahNBR","in July, August, September"],["en octobre, en novembre, en décembre","ahn ohktoHBR ahn nohvahNBR ahn daysahNBR","in October, November, December"],["au printemps, en été, en automne, en hiver","oh prantahNPS ahn ayTAY ahn ohtoHNN ahn eevUHR","in spring, summer, autumn, winter"]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"Il ___ beau aujourd'hui.","a":"fait"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Il ___ . Prends un parapluie.","a":"pleut"},{"t":"choice","q":"in winter","opts":["au hiver","en hiver"],"a":"en hiver"},{"t":"choice","q":"in spring","opts":["en printemps","au printemps"],"a":"au printemps"},{"t":"translate","q":"It's cold in January.","a":"Il fait froid en janvier."}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-31","label":"Chapitre 31","name":"Du, de la, des","summary":"The partitive: some bread, some water, some friends.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Le partitif","note":"Use <strong>du, de la, de l', des</strong> for an unspecified amount. After a negative or a quantity word it becomes <strong>de</strong>. After aimer / adorer / détester / préférer, French prefers the definite article: j'aime le fromage.","items":[["Je prends du café.","zhuh prahNDS dew kahFAY","I'll have some coffee."],["Elle mange de la salade.","ell mahNZH duh lah sahlAHD","She's eating some salad."],["Tu veux de l'eau ?","tew vuh duh loh","Do you want some water?"],["Il achète des pommes.","eel ahshEHT day poHNM","He buys some apples."],["Je ne veux pas de café.","zhuh nuh vuh pah duh kahFAY","I don't want any coffee."],["beaucoup de pain","bohKOO duh pan","a lot of bread"],["J'aime le fromage.","zhem luh frohmaHZH","I like cheese."],["Nous prenons de la tarte.","noo pruhnoHNS duh lah taHRT","We'll have some tart."]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"Je voudrais ___ pain.","a":"du"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Elle boit ___ eau.","a":"de l'","alt":["de l'"]},{"t":"cloze","q":"Il achète ___ oranges.","a":"des"},{"t":"choice","q":"I like coffee (in general).","opts":["J'aime du café.","J'aime le café."],"a":"J'aime le café."},{"t":"translate","q":"I don't want any meat.","a":"Je ne veux pas de viande."}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-32","label":"Chapitre 32","name":"Un litre de, beaucoup de, pas de","summary":"Quantity words always take de.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Les quantités","note":"After a quantity, use <strong>de</strong> even in the plural: beaucoup de, un peu de, trop de, assez de, un kilo de, une bouteille de, un morceau de, une tranche de.","items":[["un litre de lait","uhn leETR duh leh","a litre of milk"],["un kilo de tomates","uhn keeLOH duh tohmAHT","a kilo of tomatoes"],["une bouteille d'eau","ewn bootEHL doh","a bottle of water"],["un morceau de fromage","uhn mohrSOH duh frohmaHZH","a piece of cheese"],["une tranche de jambon","ewn trahNSH duh zhahnbOHN","a slice of ham"],["beaucoup de travail","bohKOO duh trahvEHL","a lot of work"],["un peu de sucre","uhn puh duh seWKR","a little sugar"],["trop de bruit","troh duh breWEE","too much noise"],["assez d'argent","ah-SAY dahRZH","enough money"],["pas de sel","pah duh suhl","no salt"]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"un kilo ___ pommes","a":"de"},{"t":"cloze","q":"beaucoup ___ amis","a":"d'","alt":["d'"]},{"t":"cloze","q":"une bouteille ___ eau","a":"d'","alt":["d'"]},{"t":"translate","q":"Too much sugar.","a":"Trop de sucre."},{"t":"choice","q":"a lot of books","opts":["beaucoup des livres","beaucoup de livres"],"a":"beaucoup de livres"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-33","label":"Chapitre 33","name":"Plus, moins, aussi… que","summary":"Comparing two people or things.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Le comparatif","note":"plus + adjective + que = more… than. moins… que = less. aussi… que = as… as. Irregular: <strong>bon → meilleur</strong>, <strong>bien → mieux</strong>. The adjective still agrees.","items":[["Paul est plus grand que Luc.","pohl eh plew grahn kuh lews","Paul is taller than Luc."],["Léa est moins bavarde que Nina.","laYAH eh mwaHNS bahvaHRD kuh neeNAH","Léa is less talkative than Nina."],["Je suis aussi fatigué que toi.","zhuh swee oh-SEE fahteeGAY kuh twah","I am as tired as you."],["Ce café est meilleur.","suh kahFAY eh mehlUHR","This coffee is better."],["Elle parle mieux français.","ell paHRL meEUH frahn-SEH","She speaks French better."],["C'est plus cher que ça.","seh plew shUHR kuh sah","That's more expensive than that."],["Il est moins patient que moi.","eel eh mwaHNS pahtyANT kuh mwah","He is less patient than I am."],["Cette tarte est meilleure.","set taHRT eh mehlUHR","This tart is better."]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"Il est plus grand ___ moi.","a":"que"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Ce gâteau est ___ que l'autre.","a":"meilleur"},{"t":"choice","q":"better (adverb)","opts":["plus bien","mieux"],"a":"mieux"},{"t":"translate","q":"She is as tall as me.","a":"Elle est aussi grande que moi."},{"t":"cloze","q":"Cette soupe est ___ (bonne).","a":"meilleure"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-34","label":"Chapitre 34","name":"Le superlatif","summary":"The most, the least, and comparing amounts.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Le plus, le moins","note":"Superlative: <strong>le / la / les plus</strong> + adjective. Irregular: le meilleur, le mieux. Amounts: plus de, moins de, autant de + noun.","items":[["C'est le plus grand musée.","seh luh plew grahn mewzaYUH","It's the biggest museum."],["C'est la plus belle place.","seh lah plew buhl plAHS","It's the most beautiful square."],["Ce sont les moins chers.","suh sohn lay mwaHNS shuHRS","They are the least expensive."],["C'est le meilleur restaurant.","seh luh mehlUHR ruhstohraHNT","It's the best restaurant."],["Il chante le mieux.","eel shaHNT luh meEUH","He sings the best."],["J'ai plus de travail que toi.","zhay plew duh trahvEHL kuh twah","I have more work than you."],["Elle a autant d'amis que lui.","ell ah ohtaHNT dahMEE kuh leWEE","She has as many friends as him."],["moins de sucre","mwaHNS duh seWKR","less sugar"]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"C'est ___ plus jolie rue.","a":"la"},{"t":"cloze","q":"C'est le ___ café du quartier.","a":"meilleur"},{"t":"choice","q":"more time","opts":["plus de temps","plus du temps"],"a":"plus de temps"},{"t":"translate","q":"It's the least expensive.","a":"C'est le moins cher."},{"t":"cloze","q":"Elle a ___ d'argent que moi.","a":"autant","hint":"as much as"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-recap4","label":"Bilan n° 4","name":"Le temps, les quantités","summary":"Dates, time, weather, partitives, quantities, comparison.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Bilan 4","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"Nous sommes le 3 ___.","a":"mars","hint":"a month, no capital"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Il est huit ___ et demie.","a":"heures"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Il ___ froid en hiver.","a":"fait"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Je voudrais ___ fromage.","a":"du"},{"t":"cloze","q":"beaucoup ___ café","a":"de"},{"t":"choice","q":"better (adjective)","opts":["plus bon","meilleur"],"a":"meilleur"},{"t":"translate","q":"It's the best.","a":"C'est le meilleur.","alt":["C'est le mieux."]},{"t":"cloze","q":"___ printemps, il pleut.","a":"Au"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-35","label":"Chapitre 35","name":"Les verbes en -ir : finir, grandir","summary":"The second regular group: -ir verbs with -iss-.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Finir, choisir, grandir","note":"Drop -ir and add is, is, it, issons, issez, issent. The participle is -i. This group includes finir, choisir, réussir, grandir, maigrir, rougir, remplir.","items":[["je finis, tu finis, il finit","zhuh feeNEE tew feeNEE eel feeNEE","I finish, you finish, he finishes"],["nous finissons, vous finissez, ils finissent","noo feeneessoHNS voo feeneESS eel feeneESS","we / you / they finish"],["Je choisis une tarte.","zhuh shwahZEE ewn taHRT","I choose a tart."],["Elle réussit l'examen.","ell rayewsSEE luhksahmAHN","She passes the exam."],["Les enfants grandissent vite.","lay ahnfahNTS grahndeESS veet","Children grow quickly."],["Tu remplis le formulaire ?","tew rahnpLEE luh fohrmewlEHR","Are you filling in the form?"],["Nous choisissons le menu.","noo shwahzeessoHNS luh muhNEW","We choose the menu."],["Ils finissent à six heures.","eel feeneESS ah see uhr","They finish at six."]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"Nous ___ (finir) à midi.","a":"finissons"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Elle ___ (choisir) une robe.","a":"choisit"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Ils ___ (grandir) vite.","a":"grandissent"},{"t":"translate","q":"I fill in the form.","a":"Je remplis le formulaire."},{"t":"choice","q":"you (vous) succeed","opts":["vous réussissez","vous réussi"],"a":"vous réussissez"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-36","label":"Chapitre 36","name":"Partir, sortir, dormir","summary":"Short -ir verbs, without -iss-.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Un petit groupe","note":"partir, sortir, dormir, sentir, mentir, servir. The singular drops the consonant before the ending: je pars, je dors, je sors. Partir and sortir (leave a place) take <strong>être</strong> in the passé composé. Sortir something takes avoir: j'ai sorti les poubelles.","items":[["je pars, tu pars, il part","zhuh paHRS tew paHRS eel paHRT","I leave"],["nous partons, vous partez, ils partent","noo pahrtoHNS voo paHRT eel paHRT","we leave"],["Je sors ce soir.","zhuh soHRS suh swAHR","I'm going out tonight."],["Tu dors ici ?","tew doHRS ee-SEE","Are you sleeping here?"],["Elle sert le café.","ell suHRT luh kahFAY","She serves the coffee."],["Je suis parti à huit heures.","zhuh swee pahrTEE ah ewee uhr","I left at eight."],["Elle est sortie.","ell eh sohrteEUH","She went out."],["J'ai dormi huit heures.","zhay dohrMEE ewee uhr","I slept eight hours."]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"Je ___ (partir) demain.","a":"pars"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Nous ___ (sortir) ce soir.","a":"sortons"},{"t":"choice","q":"She left (went away).","opts":["Elle a parti.","Elle est partie."],"a":"Elle est partie."},{"t":"cloze","q":"Tu ___ (dormir) bien ?","a":"dors"},{"t":"translate","q":"They are leaving.","a":"Ils partent."}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-37","label":"Chapitre 37","name":"Écrire et les verbes en -re","summary":"Regular-ish -re verbs, and écrire.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Attendre, vendre, écrire","note":"For attendre, vendre, perdre, répondre, rendre: je attends → j'attends, il attend (no -t extra), nous attendons. Participle -u. Écrire: j'écris, nous écrivons, écrit. Lire: je lis, nous lisons, lu.","items":[["j'attends, tu attends, il attend","zhahttahNDS tew ahttahNDS eel ahttaHND","I wait"],["nous attendons, vous attendez, ils attendent","noo ahttahndoHNS voo ahttaHND eel ahttaHND","we wait"],["J'écris un mail.","zhaykREE uhn mehl","I'm writing an email."],["Nous écrivons souvent.","noo aykreevoHNS soov","We write often."],["Elle lit le journal.","ell lee luh zhoornAHL","She reads the paper."],["Il vend sa voiture.","eel vaHND sah vwahtEWR","He's selling his car."],["Je réponds au message.","zhuh raypohNDS oh muhssaHZH","I answer the message."],["Tu perds toujours tes clés.","tew puhRDS too-ZHOOR tay klAYS","You always lose your keys."]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"J'___ (attendre) le bus.","a":"attends"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Il ___ (vendre) son vélo.","a":"vend"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Nous ___ (écrire) une carte.","a":"écrivons"},{"t":"translate","q":"She reads a lot.","a":"Elle lit beaucoup."},{"t":"choice","q":"they lose","opts":["ils perdent","ils perdons"],"a":"ils perdent"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-38","label":"Chapitre 38","name":"Savoir, connaître, croire, voir","summary":"Four verbs learners mix up, especially savoir and connaître.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Deux verbes pour know","note":"<strong>Savoir</strong> + infinitive or a fact: je sais nager, je sais que… <strong>Connaître</strong> + a person or a place: je connais Paris. Croire = believe. Voir = see. Participles: su, connu, cru, vu.","items":[["Je sais nager.","zhuh seh nahzhUHR","I can swim."],["Tu sais où il habite ?","tew seh oo eel ahbEET","Do you know where he lives?"],["Je connais ton frère.","zhuh kohnNEH tohn frEHR","I know your brother."],["Elle connaît bien Lyon.","ell kohnNEH byan leeOHN","She knows Lyon well."],["Je crois que oui.","zhuh krWAH kuh wee","I think so."],["Tu vois la mer ?","tew vwah lah muhr","Can you see the sea?"],["Nous voyons un film.","noo voheeoHNS uhn feELM","We're seeing a film."],["Je ne crois pas.","zhuh nuh krWAH pah","I don't think so."]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"choice","q":"I know this city.","opts":["Je sais cette ville.","Je connais cette ville."],"a":"Je connais cette ville."},{"t":"choice","q":"I know how to drive.","opts":["Je sais conduire.","Je connais conduire."],"a":"Je sais conduire."},{"t":"cloze","q":"Je ne ___ pas. (croire)","a":"crois"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Tu ___ la gare ? (voir)","a":"vois"},{"t":"translate","q":"She knows my mother.","a":"Elle connaît ma mère."}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-39","label":"Chapitre 39","name":"Boire","summary":"Boire has three stems: boi-, boiv-, buv-.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Je bois, nous buvons","note":"Singular bois / boit, plural buvons / buvez, and ils boivent. Participle bu. Future boirai.","items":[["je bois","zhuh bwah","I drink"],["tu bois","tew bwah","you drink"],["il boit","eel bwah","he drinks"],["nous buvons","noo bewvoHNS","we drink"],["vous buvez","voo bewv","you drink"],["ils boivent","eel bwAHV","they drink"],["Je bois de l'eau.","zhuh bwah duh loh","I drink water."],["Qu'est-ce que vous buvez ?","kess-kuh voo bewv","What are you drinking?"],["Elle a bu un café.","ell ah bew uhn kahFAY","She drank a coffee."]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"Nous ___ (boire) un thé.","a":"buvons"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Ils ___ (boire) du vin.","a":"boivent"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Elle ___ (boire) un jus.","a":"boit"},{"t":"translate","q":"What are you drinking?","a":"Qu'est-ce que tu bois ?","alt":["Qu'est-ce que vous buvez ?"]},{"t":"choice","q":"past participle","opts":["buvé","bu","boit"],"a":"bu"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-40","label":"Chapitre 40","name":"Vouloir, pouvoir, devoir","summary":"Want, can, must — and the polite conditional.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Trois verbes modaux","note":"je veux / je peux / je dois. The plural stem changes: voulons, pouvons, devons. For a polite request use the conditional, not the present: <strong>je voudrais</strong>, <strong>je pourrais</strong>. Devoir in the present is an obligation now.","items":[["Je veux un café.","zhuh vuh uhn kahFAY","I want a coffee."],["Je voudrais un café, s'il vous plaît.","zhuh voodREH uhn kahFAY seel voo PLEH","I'd like a coffee, please."],["Tu peux m'aider ?","tew puh mehdUHR","Can you help me?"],["Je peux entrer ?","zhuh puh ahntrUHR","May I come in?"],["Je dois partir.","zhuh dwah pahrtEER","I have to leave."],["Nous devons réserver.","noo duhvoHNS rayzuhrvUHR","We have to book."],["Elle ne peut pas venir.","ell nuh puh pah vuhnEER","She can't come."],["Vous voulez goûter ?","voo vool gootUHR","Do you want to taste it?"]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"choice","q":"Polite, in a café.","opts":["Je veux un thé.","Je voudrais un thé."],"a":"Je voudrais un thé."},{"t":"cloze","q":"Tu ___ (pouvoir) venir ?","a":"peux"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Je ___ (devoir) travailler.","a":"dois"},{"t":"translate","q":"She can't come.","a":"Elle ne peut pas venir."},{"t":"cloze","q":"Nous ___ (vouloir) partir.","a":"voulons"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-41","label":"Chapitre 41","name":"Faire et dire","summary":"Two very frequent irregulars, including vous faites and vous dites.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Faire, dire","note":"faire: je fais, nous faisons, vous faites, ils font. Participle fait. dire: je dis, nous disons, vous dites, ils disent. Participle dit. Faire is also in weather and many set phrases: faire les courses, faire attention.","items":[["je fais, tu fais, il fait","zhuh feh tew feh eel feh","I do / make"],["nous faisons, vous faites, ils font","noo fehzoHNS voo feht eel foHNT","we do, you do, they do"],["je dis, tu dis, il dit","zhuh dee tew dee eel dee","I say"],["nous disons, vous dites, ils disent","noo deezoHNS voo deet eel dees","we say, you say, they say"],["Je fais les courses.","zhuh feh lay koORS","I do the shopping."],["Qu'est-ce que tu fais ?","kess-kuh tew feh","What are you doing?"],["Elle dit bonjour.","ell dee bohn-ZHOOR","She says hello."],["Faites attention !","feht ahttahnteeOHN","Be careful!"]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"Vous ___ (faire) du sport ?","a":"faites"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Ils ___ (faire) un gâteau.","a":"font"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Vous ___ (dire) ça souvent.","a":"dites"},{"t":"choice","q":"they say","opts":["ils disent","ils disont"],"a":"ils disent"},{"t":"translate","q":"What are you doing?","a":"Qu'est-ce que tu fais ?","alt":["Qu'est-ce que vous faites ?"]}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-42","label":"Chapitre 42","name":"Aller","summary":"Aller in the present, the base of the near future.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Je vais, tu vas, il va","note":"vais, vas, va, allons, allez, vont. Passé composé with être: je suis allé. The near future is aller + infinitive, taught properly in chapter 43.","items":[["je vais","zhuh veh","I go"],["tu vas","tew vah","you go"],["il va / elle va","eel vah / ell vah","he / she goes"],["nous allons","noo ahloHNS","we go"],["vous allez","voo ahl","you go"],["ils vont","eel voHNT","they go"],["Je vais à la piscine.","zhuh veh ah lah peesSAN","I'm going to the pool."],["On va au marché ?","ohn vah oh mahrsHAY","Shall we go to the market?"],["Elle est allée à Nice.","ell eh ahlaYUH ah nees","She went to Nice."],["Vous allez bien ?","voo ahl byan","Are you well?"]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"Je ___ au travail.","a":"vais"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Ils ___ à l'école.","a":"vont"},{"t":"choice","q":"She went to Lyon.","opts":["Elle a allé à Lyon.","Elle est allée à Lyon."],"a":"Elle est allée à Lyon."},{"t":"translate","q":"We are going to the cinema.","a":"Nous allons au cinéma."},{"t":"cloze","q":"Tu ___ où ?","a":"vas"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-recap5","label":"Bilan n° 5","name":"Les verbes du présent","summary":"A mixed present-tense check before the past and the future.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Bilan 5","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"Nous ___ (finir) tard.","a":"finissons"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Je ___ (partir) maintenant.","a":"pars"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Elle ___ (boire) un thé.","a":"boit"},{"t":"choice","q":"I know Paris.","opts":["Je sais Paris.","Je connais Paris."],"a":"Je connais Paris."},{"t":"cloze","q":"Vous ___ (faire) la cuisine ?","a":"faites"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Ils ___ (aller) au stade.","a":"vont"},{"t":"translate","q":"I'd like a coffee.","a":"Je voudrais un café."},{"t":"choice","q":"She left.","opts":["Elle a parti.","Elle est partie."],"a":"Elle est partie."}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-43","label":"Chapitre 43","name":"Le futur proche","summary":"Aller + infinitive: what you are about to do.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Je vais partir","note":"Conjugate <strong>aller</strong> and leave the second verb in the infinitive. Use it for plans and the immediate future. Negation wraps aller: je ne vais pas sortir.","items":[["Je vais manger.","zhuh veh mahnzhUHR","I'm going to eat."],["Tu vas faire quoi ?","tew vah fehr kwah","What are you going to do?"],["Il va pleuvoir.","eel vah pluhvwAHR","It's going to rain."],["Nous allons visiter le musée.","noo ahloHNS veezeetUHR luh mewzaYUH","We're going to visit the museum."],["Vous allez aimer.","voo ahl ehmUHR","You're going to like it."],["Ils vont déménager.","eel voHNT daymaynahzhUHR","They're going to move."],["Je ne vais pas travailler demain.","zhuh nuh veh pah trahvehlUHR duh-MAN","I'm not going to work tomorrow."],["On va prendre un café ?","ohn vah prahNDR uhn kahFAY","Shall we get a coffee?"]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"Je vais ___ (partir) à six heures.","a":"partir"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Elle ___ visiter sa mère.","a":"va"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Nous ___ réserver une table.","a":"allons"},{"t":"translate","q":"I'm not going to come.","a":"Je ne vais pas venir."},{"t":"choice","q":"They're going to sleep.","opts":["Ils vont dormir.","Ils vont dormtent."],"a":"Ils vont dormir."}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-44","label":"Chapitre 44","name":"Le passé composé avec avoir : verbes en -er","summary":"The past tense for a finished event, regular -er verbs.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"J'ai parlé","note":"avoir in the present + past participle. For -er verbs the participle is -é, and it does <strong>not</strong> agree with the subject. Negation: je n'ai pas parlé. Questions: est-ce que tu as parlé ? Time words: hier, ce matin, la semaine dernière, il y a deux jours.","items":[["J'ai travaillé hier.","zhay trahvehLAY yehr","I worked yesterday."],["Tu as regardé le match ?","tew ah ruhgahrDAY luh mahTSH","Did you watch the match?"],["Elle a habité à Nice.","ell ah ahbeeTAY ah nees","She lived in Nice."],["Nous avons mangé tôt.","noo ah-VOHN mahnzHAY toht","We ate early."],["Vous avez aimé le film ?","voo ah-VAY ehMAY luh feELM","Did you like the film?"],["Ils ont visité le Louvre.","eel ohn veezeeTAY luh loOVR","They visited the Louvre."],["Je n'ai pas écouté.","zhuh nay pah aykooTAY","I didn't listen."],["Il y a une heure, j'ai téléphoné.","eel ee ah ewn uhr zhay taylayfohNAY","An hour ago, I phoned."]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"J'ai ___ (parler) avec Léa.","a":"parlé"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Nous avons ___ (manger) une pizza.","a":"mangé"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Elle n'a pas ___ (aimer) le film.","a":"aimé"},{"t":"translate","q":"I worked yesterday.","a":"J'ai travaillé hier."},{"t":"choice","q":"Did you watch?","opts":["Est-ce que tu as regardé ?","Est-ce que tu as regarder ?"],"a":"Est-ce que tu as regardé ?"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-45","label":"Chapitre 45","name":"Le passé composé avec avoir : les autres","summary":"Participles of -ir, -re and the irregulars.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Les participes","note":"-ir → -i (fini, choisi, dormi). Many -re → -u (vendu, attendu, perdu, répondu). Learn the irregulars as pairs: faire/fait, dire/dit, écrire/écrit, lire/lu, boire/bu, voir/vu, prendre/pris, mettre/mis, avoir/eu, être/été.","items":[["J'ai fini.","zhay feeNEE","I have finished."],["Elle a choisi une robe.","ell ah shwahZEE ewn rohb","She chose a dress."],["Nous avons attendu.","noo ah-VOHN ahttahnDEW","We waited."],["Tu as vu ce film ?","tew ah vew suh feELM","Have you seen this film?"],["Il a pris le train.","eel ah pree luh tran","He took the train."],["J'ai mis mon manteau.","zhay mee mohn mahnTOH","I put my coat on."],["Elle a écrit une carte.","ell ah aykREE ewn kaHRT","She wrote a card."],["Vous avez dit ça ?","voo ah-VAY dee sah","Did you say that?"],["J'ai bu un café.","zhay bew uhn kahFAY","I drank a coffee."],["Ils ont fait les courses.","eel ohn feh lay koORS","They did the shopping."]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"J'ai ___ (prendre) le bus.","a":"pris"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Elle a ___ (voir) Paul.","a":"vu"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Nous avons ___ (faire) un gâteau.","a":"fait"},{"t":"choice","q":"I wrote","opts":["J'ai écrivé.","J'ai écrit."],"a":"J'ai écrit."},{"t":"translate","q":"She drank a tea.","a":"Elle a bu un thé."}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-46","label":"Chapitre 46","name":"Le passé composé avec être","summary":"Movement verbs and all pronominal verbs agree.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Je suis allé, je suis allée","note":"A small set takes être: aller, venir, arriver, partir, entrer, sortir, monter, descendre, naître, mourir, rester, tomber, retourner, and passer when it means 'go past'. The participle agrees with the subject. All pronominal verbs take être: je me suis levé(e). The negative wraps the auxiliary: je ne suis pas parti.","items":[["Je suis allé au marché.","zhuh swee ahLAY oh mahrsHAY","I went to the market. (man)"],["Je suis allée au marché.","zhuh swee ahlaYUH oh mahrsHAY","I went to the market. (woman)"],["Elle est arrivée en retard.","ell eh ahrreevaYUH ahn ruhtaHRD","She arrived late."],["Nous sommes partis à midi.","noo sum pahrTEE ah meeDEE","We left at noon."],["Ils sont restés à la maison.","eel sohn ruhstAYS ah lah mehzOHN","They stayed home."],["Tu es tombé ?","tew eh tohnBAY","Did you fall?"],["Je me suis levé à sept heures.","zhuh muh swee luhVAY ah suHPT uhr","I got up at seven."],["Elle s'est couchée tard.","ell seh kooshaYUH taHRD","She went to bed late."],["Je ne suis pas sorti.","zhuh nuh swee pah sohrTEE","I didn't go out."]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"choice","q":"Marie went out.","opts":["Marie a sorti.","Marie est sortie."],"a":"Marie est sortie."},{"t":"cloze","q":"Nous sommes ___ (arriver) hier.","a":"arrivés","alt":["arrivé(e)s"]},{"t":"cloze","q":"Elle est ___ (partir) à huit heures.","a":"partie"},{"t":"translate","q":"I got up at 7. (woman speaking)","a":"Je me suis levée à sept heures.","alt":["Je me suis levée à 7 heures."]},{"t":"choice","q":"They (women) stayed.","opts":["Elles sont resté.","Elles sont restées."],"a":"Elles sont restées."}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-47","label":"Chapitre 47","name":"L'imparfait","summary":"Background, habit, and description in the past.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Je parlais, il faisait beau","note":"Take the nous form of the present, drop -ons, add ais, ais, ait, ions, iez, aient. Only être is irregular: j'étais. Use the imparfait for weather, age, descriptions, and what used to happen. Use the passé composé for the event that happened once.","items":[["nous parlons → je parlais","noo pahrloHNS → zhuh pahrLEH","the stem is parl-"],["Il faisait beau.","eel fehZEH boh","The weather was nice."],["Elle avait vingt ans.","ell ahVEH vaNGT ahns","She was twenty."],["J'habitais à Lyon.","zhahbeeTEH ah leeOHN","I used to live in Lyon."],["Tous les dimanches, on allait chez ma grand-mère.","toos lay deemahNSH ohn ahLEH shay mah grahnd-mEHR","Every Sunday we went to my grandmother's."],["Je lisais quand tu as téléphoné.","zhuh leeZEH kaHND tew ah taylayfohNAY","I was reading when you phoned."],["C'était super.","sayTEH sewpUHR","It was great."],["Nous étions fatigués.","noo ayteeoHNS fahteegAYS","We were tired."]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"Je ___ (habiter) à Nice avant.","a":"habitais"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Il ___ (faire) froid.","a":"faisait"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Nous ___ (être) en retard.","a":"étions"},{"t":"choice","q":"A habit in the past.","opts":["Tous les jours, je prenais le bus.","Hier, j'ai pris le bus."],"a":"Tous les jours, je prenais le bus."},{"t":"translate","q":"She was tired.","a":"Elle était fatiguée."}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-48","label":"Chapitre 48","name":"Le futur simple","summary":"Will: the infinitive plus ai, as, a, ons, ez, ont.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Je parlerai","note":"For -er and -ir, add the endings to the infinitive. Drop the final e of -re verbs: je vendrai. Irregular stems to learn: ir-, ser-, aur-, fer-, saur-, pourr-, voudr-, verr-, enverr-, viendr-, recevr-. Used for a promise, a prediction, or a plan that is not immediate.","items":[["je parlerai, tu parleras, il parlera","zhuh pahrluhREH tew pahrluhRAH eel pahrluhRAH","I will speak"],["nous finirons, vous finirez, ils finiront","noo feeneeroHNS voo feenEER eel feeneeroHNT","we will finish"],["Je serai là.","zhuh suhREH lah","I will be there."],["Il aura vingt ans.","eel ohRAH vaNGT ahns","He will be twenty."],["Nous irons en Italie.","noo eeroHNS ahn eetahleEUH","We will go to Italy."],["Elle fera un gâteau.","ell fuhRAH uhn gahTOH","She will make a cake."],["Tu verras.","tew vuhrRAH","You'll see."],["Ils viendront demain.","eel vyandroHNT duh-MAN","They will come tomorrow."]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"Je ___ (être) là à huit heures.","a":"serai"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Nous ___ (aller) à Lille.","a":"irons"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Elle ___ (faire) les courses.","a":"fera"},{"t":"translate","q":"I will call you.","a":"Je t'appellerai.","alt":["Je vous appellerai."]},{"t":"choice","q":"you will have","opts":["tu auras","tu avoiras"],"a":"tu auras"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-49","label":"Chapitre 49","name":"Présent, passé, futur","summary":"Choosing the tense in one short story.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Trois moments","note":"Present: now or a habit. Passé composé: a finished event. Imparfait: the background around that event. Futur proche: a plan already in motion. Futur simple: will, a bit further away.","items":[["Aujourd'hui, je travaille.","oh-zhoor-DWEE zhuh trahvEHL","Today I'm working."],["Hier, j'ai travaillé.","yehr zhay trahvehLAY","Yesterday I worked."],["Avant, je travaillais le samedi.","ah-VAHN zhuh trahvehLEH luh sahmuhDEE","I used to work on Saturdays."],["Demain, je vais me reposer.","duh-MAN zhuh veh muh ruhpohzUHR","Tomorrow I'm going to rest."],["L'année prochaine, j'habiterai à Bordeaux.","lahnnaYUH prohsHAN zhahbeetuhREH ah bohrDOH","Next year I'll live in Bordeaux."],["Il pleuvait et j'ai pris un taxi.","eel pluhVEH ay zhay pree uhn tahkSEE","It was raining and I took a taxi."],["Quand j'étais petit, je lisais beaucoup.","kaHND zhayTEH puh-TEE zhuh leeZEH bohKOO","When I was little, I read a lot."],["Ce soir, on va sortir.","suh swAHR ohn vah sohrtEER","Tonight we're going out."]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"choice","q":"A finished event yesterday.","opts":["Hier je mangeais une pizza.","Hier j'ai mangé une pizza."],"a":"Hier j'ai mangé une pizza."},{"t":"choice","q":"Background weather.","opts":["Il a plu et j'ai couru.","Il pleuvait quand je suis sorti."],"a":"Il pleuvait quand je suis sorti."},{"t":"cloze","q":"Demain, je ___ partir tôt. (near future)","a":"vais"},{"t":"translate","q":"Next year I will be in Paris.","a":"L'année prochaine, je serai à Paris."},{"t":"cloze","q":"Avant, elle ___ (habiter) ici.","a":"habitait"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-recap6","label":"Bilan n° 6","name":"Les temps","summary":"Near future, passé composé, imparfait, futur simple.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Bilan 6","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"Je vais ___ (sortir).","a":"sortir"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Nous avons ___ (prendre) le train.","a":"pris"},{"t":"choice","q":"She arrived.","opts":["Elle a arrivé.","Elle est arrivée."],"a":"Elle est arrivée."},{"t":"cloze","q":"Il ___ (faire) beau. (background)","a":"faisait"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Vous ___ (être) là demain.","a":"serez"},{"t":"translate","q":"I didn't go out.","a":"Je ne suis pas sorti.","alt":["Je ne suis pas sortie."]},{"t":"choice","q":"a habit before","opts":["Je prenais le bus.","J'ai pris le bus une fois."],"a":"Je prenais le bus."},{"t":"cloze","q":"Elles se sont ___ (lever) tard.","a":"levées"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-50","label":"Chapitre 50","name":"Il y a, pendant, depuis, dans","summary":"How long, since when, and in how long.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"La durée","note":"<strong>il y a</strong> + time = ago. <strong>pendant</strong> = for a finished period. <strong>depuis</strong> = since, still true, with the present. <strong>dans</strong> = in, counting forward. Don't use il y a for the future.","items":[["Je suis arrivé il y a dix minutes.","zhuh swee ahrreeVAY eel ee ah dee meenEWT","I arrived ten minutes ago."],["J'ai habité là pendant deux ans.","zhay ahbeeTAY lah pahn-DAHN duh ahns","I lived there for two years."],["J'habite ici depuis 2020.","zhah-BEET ee-SEE duh-PWEE 2020","I have lived here since 2020."],["J'apprends le français depuis six mois.","zhahpprahNDS luh frahn-SEH duh-PWEE see mwah","I have been learning French for six months."],["Le train part dans une heure.","luh tran paHRT dahn ewn uhr","The train leaves in an hour."],["Je te rappelle dans cinq minutes.","zhuh tuh rahppUHL dahn sanq meenEWT","I'll call you back in five minutes."],["Depuis quand tu es là ?","duh-PWEE kaHND tew eh lah","How long have you been here?"],["Il y a longtemps.","eel ee ah lohngtahNPS","A long time ago."]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"choice","q":"ago","opts":["Je suis parti depuis une heure.","Je suis parti il y a une heure."],"a":"Je suis parti il y a une heure."},{"t":"choice","q":"still true","opts":["J'habite ici depuis mai.","J'habite ici pendant mai."],"a":"J'habite ici depuis mai."},{"t":"cloze","q":"Le film commence ___ dix minutes.","a":"dans"},{"t":"translate","q":"I lived there for three years.","a":"J'ai habité là pendant trois ans."},{"t":"cloze","q":"___ quand est-ce que tu apprends le français ?","a":"Depuis"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-51","label":"Chapitre 51","name":"Où, quand, comment","summary":"The three question words for place, time and manner.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Trois questions","note":"où = where, quand = when, comment = how. They can sit at the start with est-ce que, or after the verb in a softer spoken question. Comment also means 'what (did you say)?'","items":[["Où tu habites ?","oo tew ahbEET","Where do you live?"],["Où est-ce que vous travaillez ?","oo ess-kuh voo trahvEHL","Where do you work?"],["Quand est-ce qu'on part ?","kaHND uhsT-S kohn paHRT","When do we leave?"],["Tu viens quand ?","tew vyANS kaHND","When are you coming?"],["Comment tu t'appelles ?","kohnmaHNT tew tahppUHL","What's your name? (literally how do you call yourself)"],["Comment allez-vous ?","kohnmaHNT ahluhz-VOO","How are you?"],["Comment ça s'écrit ?","kohnmaHNT sah saykREE","How is that spelled?"],["D'où tu viens ?","doo tew vyANS","Where are you from?"]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"___ est la gare ?","a":"Où"},{"t":"cloze","q":"___ est-ce qu'on mange ?","a":"Quand","alt":["Où"]},{"t":"cloze","q":"___ vous appelez-vous ?","a":"Comment"},{"t":"translate","q":"Where do you live?","a":"Où habites-tu ?","alt":["Où est-ce que tu habites ?","Tu habites où ?"]},{"t":"choice","q":"How are you?","opts":["Comment allez-vous ?","Quand allez-vous ?"],"a":"Comment allez-vous ?"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-52","label":"Chapitre 52","name":"Qui, qu'est-ce que, quel","summary":"Asking about a person, a thing, and a choice.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Qui, que, quel","note":"<strong>qui</strong> = who. <strong>qu'est-ce que</strong> + subject = what (object). <strong>quel / quelle / quels / quelles</strong> agrees with the noun and asks 'which'. Don't confuse quel (which) with qu'est-ce que (what).","items":[["Qui est-ce ?","kee uhsT-S","Who is it?"],["Qui tu invites ?","kee tew anvEET","Who are you inviting?"],["Qu'est-ce que tu veux ?","kess-kuh tew vuh","What do you want?"],["Qu'est-ce qui se passe ?","kess-kee suh paHSS","What's happening?"],["Quel âge as-tu ?","kuhl ahzh ahs-TEW","How old are you?"],["Quelle heure est-il ?","kuhl uhr uhst-EEL","What time is it?"],["Quels films tu aimes ?","kuHLS feeLMS tew an","Which films do you like?"],["Quelle est votre adresse ?","kuhl eh VOH-truh ahdruHSS","What is your address?"]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"___ heure est-il ?","a":"Quelle"},{"t":"cloze","q":"___ est-ce que tu lis ?","a":"Qu'"},{"t":"choice","q":"Which (feminine singular) city?","opts":["Quel ville ?","Quelle ville ?"],"a":"Quelle ville ?"},{"t":"translate","q":"What do you want?","a":"Qu'est-ce que tu veux ?","alt":["Qu'est-ce que vous voulez ?"]},{"t":"cloze","q":"___ âge as-tu ?","a":"Quel"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-53","label":"Chapitre 53","name":"Ne… rien, jamais, plus, personne","summary":"The other negatives.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Pas n'est pas seul","note":"ne… pas = not. ne… jamais = never. ne… plus = no longer. ne… rien = nothing. ne… personne = nobody. Personne and rien can be the subject: personne n'est venu, rien ne marche. In the passé composé, the second half sits between the auxiliary and the participle: je n'ai rien dit.","items":[["Je ne fume jamais.","zhuh nuh fuhn zhah-MEH","I never smoke."],["Il ne travaille plus ici.","eel nuh trahvEHL plew ee-SEE","He doesn't work here any more."],["Je ne comprends rien.","zhuh nuh kohnprahNDS ryan","I don't understand anything."],["Elle ne voit personne.","ell nuh vwah puhrsoHNN","She doesn't see anyone."],["Personne ne répond.","puhrsoHNN nuh raypoHND","Nobody answers."],["Rien n'est ouvert.","ryan neh oovuHRT","Nothing is open."],["Je n'ai rien mangé.","zhuh nay ryan mahnzHAY","I didn't eat anything."],["Tu n'es jamais allé à Nice ?","tew neh zhah-MEH ahLAY ah nees","Have you never been to Nice?"]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"Je ne bois ___ de café le soir.","a":"jamais"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Il n'habite ___ ici.","a":"plus"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Je n'ai ___ compris.","a":"rien"},{"t":"choice","q":"Nobody came.","opts":["Personne n'est venu.","Ne personne est venu."],"a":"Personne n'est venu."},{"t":"translate","q":"I didn't say anything.","a":"Je n'ai rien dit."}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-54","label":"Chapitre 54","name":"Négation et question au passé composé","summary":"Putting a past sentence into the negative or into a question.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Autour de l'auxiliaire","note":"The auxiliary carries the tense. Ne and the question both attach to it. Inversion: as-tu parlé, est-elle partie, a-t-il vu. With être, agreement stays on the participle.","items":[["J'ai vu Paul. → Je n'ai pas vu Paul.","zhay vew pohl → zhuh nay pah vew pohl","I didn't see Paul."],["Est-ce que tu as fini ?","ess-kuh tew ah feeNEE","Have you finished?"],["As-tu réservé ?","ahs-TEW rayzuhrVAY","Did you book?"],["Elle est partie ? / Est-elle partie ?","ell eh pahrteEUH / uhst-UHL pahrteEUH","Did she leave?"],["Pourquoi est-ce que vous avez choisi Lyon ?","poorkWAH ess-kuh voo ah-VAY shwahZEE leeOHN","Why did you choose Lyon?"],["Je n'ai jamais visité Marseille.","zhuh nay zhah-MEH veezeeTAY mahrsEHL","I have never visited Marseille."],["Il n'est pas encore arrivé.","eel neh pah ahn-KOR ahrreeVAY","He hasn't arrived yet."],["Qu'est-ce que tu as fait ?","kess-kuh tew ah feh","What did you do?"]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"Je n'___ pas compris.","a":"ai"},{"t":"choice","q":"Did she leave?","opts":["A-t-elle parti ?","Est-elle partie ?"],"a":"Est-elle partie ?"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Qu'est-ce que tu as ___ (faire) ?","a":"fait"},{"t":"translate","q":"I have never been to Bordeaux.","a":"Je ne suis jamais allé à Bordeaux.","alt":["Je ne suis jamais allée à Bordeaux."]},{"t":"cloze","q":"___-tu réservé une table ?","a":"As"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-recap7","label":"Bilan n° 7","name":"Questions et négation","summary":"Question words, and the family of ne…","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Bilan 7","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"___ tu habites ?","a":"Où"},{"t":"cloze","q":"___ heure est-il ?","a":"Quelle"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Je ne mange ___ de viande.","a":"jamais","hint":"never"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Elle n'a ___ dit.","a":"rien"},{"t":"choice","q":"Nobody is here.","opts":["Personne n'est là.","Il n'y a ne personne."],"a":"Personne n'est là."},{"t":"translate","q":"What did you do?","a":"Qu'est-ce que tu as fait ?","alt":["Qu'est-ce que vous avez fait ?"]},{"t":"cloze","q":"Je suis arrivé ___ deux heures. (ago)","a":"il y a"},{"t":"cloze","q":"J'habite ici ___ 2019.","a":"depuis"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-55","label":"Chapitre 55","name":"Le pronom en","summary":"En replaces de + thing, a quantity, or a place you come from.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"J'en veux","note":"<strong>En</strong> replaces de + noun: tu veux du café ? j'en veux. It also replaces a number: tu as des frères ? j'en ai deux. And a place after venir / revenir: tu viens de Lyon ? j'en viens. En sits before the verb, and before the auxiliary in the passé composé.","items":[["Tu veux du pain ? — Oui, j'en veux.","tew vuh dew pan — wee zhahn vuh","Yes, I want some."],["Tu as des sœurs ? — J'en ai deux.","tew ah day suheWRS — zhahn ay duh","I have two."],["Il n'en a pas.","eel nahn ah pah","He doesn't have any."],["Vous en voulez ?","voo ahn vool","Would you like some?"],["J'en ai pris trois.","zhahn ay pree trWAH","I took three of them."],["Tu viens du bureau ? — J'en viens.","tew vyANS dew bewROH — zhahn vyANS","I'm coming from there."],["On en parle demain.","ohn ahn paHRL duh-MAN","We'll talk about it tomorrow."],["Je n'en sais rien.","zhuh nahn seh ryan","I don't know anything about it."]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"Tu veux du café ? — Oui, j'___ veux.","a":"en"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Des frères ? J'en ai ___.","a":"deux","hint":"a number is fine"},{"t":"choice","q":"I don't have any.","opts":["Je n'en ai pas.","Je ne en ai pas."],"a":"Je n'en ai pas."},{"t":"translate","q":"I'll take two.","a":"J'en prends deux.","alt":["Je vais en prendre deux."]},{"t":"cloze","q":"Elle ___ a mangé. (some)","a":"en"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-56","label":"Chapitre 56","name":"Le pronom y","summary":"Y replaces à + place, or à + thing.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"J'y vais","note":"<strong>Y</strong> replaces à / dans / sur / chez + a place: tu vas à Paris ? j'y vais. It also replaces à + a thing: tu penses à l'examen ? j'y pense. People take a stressed pronoun instead: je pense à elle, not j'y pense. Y sits in the same slot as en.","items":[["Tu vas au marché ? — J'y vais.","tew vah oh mahrsHAY — zhee veh","I'm going there."],["Elle est à Lyon ? — Oui, elle y est.","ell eh ah leeOHN — wee ell ee eh","Yes, she's there."],["On y mange bien.","ohn ee mahNZH byan","The food is good there."],["Je n'y suis jamais allé.","zhuh nee swee zhah-MEH ahLAY","I've never been there."],["Tu penses à tes vacances ? — J'y pense.","tew paHNS ah tay vahkaHNS — zhee paHNS","I'm thinking about them."],["Je réponds au mail. J'y réponds.","zhuh raypohNDS oh mehl zhee raypohNDS","I'm answering it."],["Il tient à ce travail. Il y tient.","eel tyANT ah suh trahvEHL eel ee tyANT","It matters to him."],["Je pense à Marie. (not y)","zhuh paHNS ah mahreEUH noh ee","I think of Marie."]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"Tu vas à Lille ? — J'___ vais demain.","a":"y"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Elle habite à Nice. Elle ___ habite depuis 2010.","a":"y"},{"t":"choice","q":"I think about Paul.","opts":["J'y pense.","Je pense à lui."],"a":"Je pense à lui."},{"t":"translate","q":"I've never been there.","a":"Je n'y suis jamais allé.","alt":["Je n'y suis jamais allée."]},{"t":"cloze","q":"On ___ mange bien, dans ce restaurant.","a":"y"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-57","label":"Chapitre 57","name":"Le, la, les","summary":"Direct object pronouns.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Je le vois","note":"le / la / l' / les replace a definite direct object. They go before the verb: je vois le film → je le vois. Before a vowel, le and la become l'. In the passé composé they go before the auxiliary, and the participle agrees with a preceding direct object: je l'ai vue.","items":[["Tu vois Paul ? — Je le vois.","tew vwah pohl — zhuh luh vwah","I see him."],["Tu connais Léa ? — Je la connais.","tew kohnNEH laYAH — zhuh lah kohnNEH","I know her."],["L'examen ? Je l'ai réussi.","luhksahmAHN zhuh lay rayewsSEE","I passed it."],["Les clés ? Je les cherche.","lay klAYS zhuh lay shuhRSH","I'm looking for them."],["Je ne le comprends pas.","zhuh nuh luh kohnprahNDS pah","I don't understand him / it."],["Vous les prenez ?","voo lay prAHN","Are you taking them?"],["Je l'ai vue hier.","zhuh lay veWUH yehr","I saw her yesterday."],["Il les a achetés.","eel lay ah ahshuhtAYS","He bought them."]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"Le film ? Je ___ regarde ce soir.","a":"le"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Marie ? Je ___ appelle.","a":"l'","alt":["l'"]},{"t":"cloze","q":"Les billets ? Je ___ ai.","a":"les"},{"t":"choice","q":"I saw her.","opts":["Je l'ai vu.","Je l'ai vue."],"a":"Je l'ai vue."},{"t":"translate","q":"I don't understand it. (masculine)","a":"Je ne le comprends pas."}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-58","label":"Chapitre 58","name":"Lui, leur","summary":"Indirect object pronouns: to him, to her, to them.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Je lui parle","note":"<strong>Lui</strong> = to him or to her. <strong>Leur</strong> = to them. They replace à + person: je parle à Paul → je lui parle. They never change for gender. In the passé composé: je lui ai parlé (no agreement — it is not a direct object).","items":[["Je parle à Léa. Je lui parle.","zhuh paHRL ah laYAH zhuh leWEE paHRL","I speak to her."],["Tu téléphones à tes parents ? Tu leur téléphones ?","tew taylayfOHN ah tay pahrahNTS tew luhr taylayfOHN","Do you phone them?"],["Je lui ai écrit.","zhuh leWEE ay aykREE","I wrote to him / her."],["Elle leur a offert un livre.","ell luhr ah ohffuHRT uhn leEVR","She gave them a book."],["Je ne lui dis rien.","zhuh nuh leWEE dee ryan","I'm not telling him / her anything."],["Vous leur répondez ?","voo luhr raypoHND","Are you answering them?"],["Donne-lui ton numéro.","dohnnuh-leWEE tohn newmayROH","Give him / her your number."],["Ne leur dis pas.","nuh luhr dee pah","Don't tell them."]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"Je parle à Marc. Je ___ parle.","a":"lui"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Elle écrit à ses amis. Elle ___ écrit.","a":"leur"},{"t":"choice","q":"I gave it to her. (no agreement)","opts":["Je lui ai donné.","Je lui ai donnée."],"a":"Je lui ai donné."},{"t":"translate","q":"Don't tell him.","a":"Ne lui dis pas."},{"t":"cloze","q":"Vous ___ avez téléphoné ? (to them)","a":"leur"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-59","label":"Chapitre 59","name":"Les pronoms toniques","summary":"Moi, toi, lui, elle, nous, vous, eux, elles — after a preposition, and for emphasis.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Chez moi, et toi ?","note":"Use the stressed set after a preposition (avec, pour, chez, sans, à), in comparisons, and to emphasise: moi, je préfère le thé. Lui and elle here are stressed, not the indirect pronoun of chapter 58 — the position tells you which.","items":[["moi, toi, lui, elle","mwah twah leWEE ell","me, you, him, her"],["nous, vous, eux, elles","noo voo uh ell","us, you, them"],["Tu viens avec moi ?","tew vyANS ah-VEK mwah","Are you coming with me?"],["C'est pour elle.","seh poor ell","It's for her."],["On habite chez eux.","ohn ahbEET shay uh","We live at their place."],["Il est plus grand que moi.","eel eh plew grahn kuh mwah","He is taller than me."],["Moi, j'aime le matin.","mwah zhem luh mahTAN","Me, I like the morning."],["Et toi ?","ay twah","And you?"]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"Tu viens avec ___ ?","a":"moi"},{"t":"cloze","q":"C'est pour ___. (for them, masculine)","a":"eux"},{"t":"choice","q":"at her place","opts":["chez elle","chez la"],"a":"chez elle"},{"t":"translate","q":"And you?","a":"Et toi ?","alt":["Et vous ?"]},{"t":"cloze","q":"Elle est plus patiente que ___.","a":"moi"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-60","label":"Chapitre 60","name":"Qui et que","summary":"Relative clauses: the person or thing who / that.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"L'homme qui parle, le livre que je lis","note":"<strong>Qui</strong> is the subject of the verb that follows: l'homme qui parle. <strong>Que</strong> (qu' before a vowel) is the object: le livre que je lis. They work for people and for things. Don't add a second pronoun: not <em>le livre que je le lis</em>.","items":[["C'est un ami qui habite à Lille.","seh uhn ahMEE kee ahbEET ah ly","He's a friend who lives in Lille."],["La femme qui parle est médecin.","lah faHNM kee paHRL eh mayduhSAN","The woman who is speaking is a doctor."],["Le film que je regarde est long.","luh feELM kuh zhuh ruhgaHRD eh lohNZH","The film I'm watching is long."],["La robe qu'elle porte est rouge.","lah rohb kell poHRT eh roOZH","The dress she's wearing is red."],["Les gens que je connais sont sympas.","lay zhaHNS kuh zhuh kohnNEH sohn sanPAH","The people I know are nice."],["Voilà le bus qui va au centre.","vwah-LAH luh bew kee vah oh sahNTR","There's the bus that goes to the centre."],["C'est le café que tu aimes.","seh luh kahFAY kuh tew an","It's the café you like."],["J'ai un frère qui travaille ici.","zhay uhn frEHR kee trahvEHL ee-SEE","I have a brother who works here."]]},{"name":"À vous de jouer","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"C'est un ami ___ habite ici.","a":"qui"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Le livre ___ je lis est drôle.","a":"que"},{"t":"cloze","q":"La chanson qu'___ écoute est belle.","a":"elle","hint":"subject of écouter"},{"t":"choice","q":"the man I see","opts":["l'homme qui je vois","l'homme que je vois"],"a":"l'homme que je vois"},{"t":"translate","q":"She's a friend who speaks French.","a":"C'est une amie qui parle français."}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-recap8","label":"Bilan n° 8","name":"Les pronoms et les relatifs","summary":"En, y, le/la/les, lui/leur, stressed pronouns, qui/que.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Bilan 8","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"Du sucre ? J'___ veux.","a":"en"},{"t":"cloze","q":"À Paris ? J'___ vais samedi.","a":"y"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Léa ? Je ___ ai vue.","a":"l'"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Je téléphone à Paul. Je ___ téléphone.","a":"lui"},{"t":"cloze","q":"C'est pour ___. (for me)","a":"moi"},{"t":"choice","q":"a friend who lives here","opts":["un ami qui habite ici","un ami que habite ici"],"a":"un ami qui habite ici"},{"t":"translate","q":"I didn't eat any.","a":"Je n'en ai pas mangé."},{"t":"cloze","q":"Les clés ___ je cherche sont ici.","a":"que"}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-talk","label":"Activités","name":"Petits dialogues","summary":"Short original exchanges that reuse the grammar of the book: être, avoir, questions, past, future.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Au café","note":"Read them aloud, then cover the French and rebuild it from the English.","items":[["Bonjour, qu'est-ce que vous prenez ?","bohn-ZHOOR kess-kuh voo prAHN","Hello, what will you have?"],["Je voudrais un café et un croissant, s'il vous plaît.","zhuh voodREH uhn kahFAY ay uhn krwahssaHNT seel voo PLEH","I'd like a coffee and a croissant, please."],["Vous voulez du sucre ?","voo vool dew seWKR","Do you want sugar?"],["Non merci, je n'en prends pas.","nohn mair-SEE zhuh nahn prahNDS pah","No thanks, I don't take any."],["Ça fait 4 euros 50.","sah feh 4 uhROH 50","That's 4 euros 50."]]},{"name":"Le week-end dernier","note":"Passé composé for the events, imparfait for the weather.","items":[["Qu'est-ce que tu as fait dimanche ?","kess-kuh tew ah feh deemahNSH","What did you do on Sunday?"],["Il faisait beau, alors je suis allé au parc.","eel fehZEH boh ah-LOR zhuh swee ahLAY oh paHRS","The weather was nice, so I went to the park."],["Tu y es allé avec qui ?","tew ee eh ahLAY ah-VEK kee","Who did you go there with?"],["Avec ma sœur. On a pris un vélo.","ah-VEK mah suhEWR ohn ah pree uhn vayLOH","With my sister. We rented a bike."],["Le soir, on a mangé chez nos parents.","luh swAHR ohn ah mahnzHAY shay noh pahrahNTS","In the evening we ate at our parents'."]]},{"name":"Reconstruire","quiz":[{"t":"translate","q":"I'd like a tea, please.","a":"Je voudrais un thé, s'il vous plaît."},{"t":"translate","q":"I don't take any.","a":"Je n'en prends pas."},{"t":"translate","q":"The weather was nice.","a":"Il faisait beau."},{"t":"cloze","q":"Je ___ allé au parc.","a":"suis"},{"t":"translate","q":"What did you do?","a":"Qu'est-ce que tu as fait ?","alt":["Qu'est-ce que vous avez fait ?"]}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]},{"id":"gr-test","label":"Test","name":"Test d'évaluation","summary":"Twenty mixed questions across the A1 grammar. Do it with the answers hidden, then mark the lesson done.","original":true,"groups":[{"name":"Test","quiz":[{"t":"cloze","q":"Je ___ (s'appeler) Léa.","a":"m'appelle"},{"t":"choice","q":"No article before a job.","opts":["Je suis un ingénieur.","Je suis ingénieur."],"a":"Je suis ingénieur."},{"t":"cloze","q":"Elle a ___ yeux bleus.","a":"les"},{"t":"cloze","q":"J'ai mal ___ dos.","a":"au"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Je n'ai pas ___ voiture.","a":"de"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Il habite ___ Japon.","a":"au"},{"t":"cloze","q":"___ un problème.","a":"Il y a","hint":"there is"},{"t":"choice","q":"She is a doctor.","opts":["C'est médecin.","Elle est médecin."],"a":"Elle est médecin."},{"t":"cloze","q":"Il est trois heures et ___.","a":"demie"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Je voudrais ___ eau.","a":"de l'","alt":["de l'"]},{"t":"cloze","q":"Ce café est ___ (bon) que l'autre.","a":"meilleur"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Nous ___ (finir) à six heures.","a":"finissons"},{"t":"choice","q":"I know how to swim.","opts":["Je connais nager.","Je sais nager."],"a":"Je sais nager."},{"t":"cloze","q":"Demain je ___ partir tôt.","a":"vais"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Hier elle a ___ (prendre) le train.","a":"pris"},{"t":"choice","q":"Paul went out.","opts":["Paul a sorti.","Paul est sorti."],"a":"Paul est sorti."},{"t":"cloze","q":"Je ne bois ___.","a":"jamais"},{"t":"cloze","q":"Du pain ? J'___ prends.","a":"en"},{"t":"cloze","q":"C'est une amie ___ habite ici.","a":"qui"},{"t":"translate","q":"I'd like a coffee, please.","a":"Je voudrais un café, s'il vous plaît."}],"note":"Type or choose the answer. Accents count, but a missing accent is marked as close and still saved."}]}]});
